{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers","id":1133232,"title":"Technocracy vs Black Spiral Dancers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-23T17:59:33-07:00","id":1133232,"title":"Technocracy vs Black Spiral Dancers?","content":"If the Technocracy notices a Level 5 Pit and realizes the threat the BSDs pose to the locals, how likely is it that they will unleash an army of magitech wielding terminators on them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T18:10:05-07:00","id":1133236,"title":"","content":"It depends a lot on whether you like Mage or Werewolf more, OP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T18:16:53-07:00","id":1133238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers#post1133232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Technocracy notices a Level 5 Pit and realizes the threat the BSDs pose to the locals, how likely is it that they will unleash an army of magitech wielding terminators on them?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Technocracy, IMHO, generally doesn't hunt supernaturals in general but only hunts Mages.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it's up to the ST and Comptroller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T19:15:44-07:00","id":1133253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133236#post1133236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends a lot on whether you like Mage or Werewolf more, OP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, which one you're using for cosmological assumptions. If you're going by Werewolf, there isn't going to be much of a Technocracy to do much against things like evil versions of the sandworms from Dune being ridden by BSDs. If you're going with Mage, it's unlikely that whatever metaphysical belief-perception that mages, and in particular the Technocracy, have put them in the same realm as the place where the BSD pits are clearly visible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T20:48:05-07:00","id":1133271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133253#post1133253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically, which one you're using for cosmological assumptions. If you're going by Werewolf, there isn't going to be much of a Technocracy to do much against things like evil versions of the sandworms from Dune being ridden by BSDs. If you're going with Mage, it's unlikely that whatever metaphysical belief-perception that mages, and in particular the Technocracy, have put them in the same realm as the place where the BSD pits are clearly visible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, the irony of the Technocracy vs. Traditions is the problem is the latter are very easy to hide. The Technocracy is really only able to strike when they're in Horizon Realms and the Traditions are taken root.<br /> <br /> If the Technocracy decides to invade the BSD then they have HIT Marks, Progenitor monsters, and so on to send as cannon fodder.<br /> <br /> Sand worms is easy to take down with airplanes and rockets.<br /> <br /> The big problem is the BSD don't suffer Paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T21:25:09-07:00","id":1133276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133271#post1133271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, the irony of the Technocracy vs. Traditions is the problem is the latter are very easy to hide. The Technocracy is really only able to strike when they're in Horizon Realms and the Traditions are taken root.<br /> <br /> If the Technocracy decides to invade the BSD then they have HIT Marks, Progenitor monsters, and so on to send as cannon fodder.</div> </div> </div> </div>True cannon fodder, that; BSDs will be using the same capacity for utterly negating technology that other Garou use, which means that all of their cannon fodder (the gibbering, broken masses that they normally send to soften up Gaian caerns) will have several turns to inflict uninterrupted ultraviolence on anything that the Technocracy sends in. The assault forces might also have the misfortune of stumbling upon toxic fungal spores, open balefire pits, or possibly even an acute angle acting as an obtuse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sand worms is easy to take down with airplanes and rockets. </div> </div> </div>Mmmmmmmmmmmmm I Don't Think So Halud. Mage exists on a level where they just don't notice the massive worm activity. Just trying to get wind of it would be a bug hunt in BSD territory. Game over, man!<br /> <br /> Also, rockets and bombs won't do much to larger thunderwyrms; the absolute smallest ones, at 25 feet long, still have a high enough Stamina that you'd need to use multiple rockets on one. Larger ones apparently ramp up Traits to a degree that such weapons won't do much but cause a local compromise in their hydrostatic skeleton, which is not good... for the one who fired on them, as they tend to spew out elemental toxin banes, and the fluid itself is apparently toxic as well. As with many things about Werewolf, this is not something that normal authorities or approaches are actually equipped to handle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The big problem is the BSD don't suffer Paradox. </div> </div> </div>BSDs, and any other monster in Werewolf, such as Grandmother Thunderwyrm, the Inquisitors, or Vhujunka.. Also, throw on the possibility of meeting corrupted Fera, and again, bug hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 08-24-2017, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T22:59:20-07:00","id":1133288,"title":"","content":"I'm not trying to undersell the Garou, just pointing out the fact the Technocracy does actually have a no-shit actual robot army and spirit-killing nuclear weapons. They also have aggravated damage inflicting bullets which work on spirits because the VE fight spirits.<br /> <br /> Mind you, it's a costly victory but the big advantage the Technocracy has is they're a global organization versus a single Hive here.<br /> <br /> The BIG problem would be, say, Pentex vs. The Union.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T05:11:49-07:00","id":1133326,"title":"","content":"To answer the specific question the OP raised:<br /> <br /> The Technocracy would level it. With ease, if cost.<br /> <br /> The key point there, is if the Union &quot;realizes the threat it poses,&quot; not any of this WtA vs. MtA stuff.<br /> <br /> Anything the Technocracy acknowledges as a threat - esp. non-mage Reality Deviants - is something then try to squash. If they realize they'd dealing with a level of threat that a level 5 pit carries, they're not going to bother with a bug hunt. They'll nuke it from orbit, just to be sure (even if they can't drop one of the spirit nukes for whatever reason). And then they'll cover it up as the government taking out a terrorist camp (which lets face it, that much BSD activity is going to make easy on them, &quot;Sorry journalists, but to avoid public panic, we can only now reveal that these terrorists were trying to establish a dirty bomb factory which is why we had to act with such overwhelming force. While the bomb making material has been secured, clean up efforts are exceeding delicate and we cannot let any civilians near the scene for safety of all involved.&quot;).<br /> <br /> The reason why the Technocracy doesn't go around doing this most of the time, is that they usually don't realize the threat involved. The &quot;good&quot; supernaturals keep themselves hidden well enough that they stay off the Union's hit list (even if they don't realize it), and frequently take out the &quot;bad&quot; supernaturals for the Technocracy anyway. As long as the fight between the Gaians and the BSDs doesn't break out into too much collateral damage into the mortal world, the Technocracy is happy to let them kill each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T07:16:26-07:00","id":1133364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133326#post1133326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (...) They'll nuke it from orbit, just to be sure (even if they can't drop one of the spirit nukes for whatever reason). (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it written anywhere when, how, and how often can the Technocracy do this (the nuking from the orbit part) ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T08:40:09-07:00","id":1133393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133288#post1133288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not trying to undersell the Garou, just pointing out the fact the Technocracy does actually have a no-shit actual robot army and spirit-killing nuclear weapons. They also have aggravated damage inflicting bullets which work on spirits because the VE fight spirits.<br /> <br /> Mind you, it's a costly victory but the big advantage the Technocracy has is they're a global organization versus a single Hive here.<br /> <br /> The BIG problem would be, say, Pentex vs. The Union.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, then the other hives would probably enter high alert, particularly other Level 5 Pits, and they would find out who did it, giving the rest of the Technocracy a rather severe problem to deal with in the future, particularly in Russia, where the BSDs have Zmei on their side.<br /> <br /> However, Pentex vs. the Union? That's a no-contest victory for Pentex. You'd have a better time convincing the Union that all members should saw off their own feet than you would convincing them that Pentex's practices are a problem. The Union eats, breaths, and sleeps the kind of reckless economic raiding that Pentex represents. The Union as a whole is so blind to its faults that the other Conventions haven't noticed anything up with the Syndicate, and the Syndicate still thinks that there's something that they can salvage from their SPD clusterfuck. When it comes to operations, the TU always yields to the purse strings. It's the fundamental reality that they've accepted as their own, and they wouldn't be able to escape from it without completely abandoning their course for the past several centuries and starting over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T08:40:56-07:00","id":1133394,"title":"","content":"In Mage Technocracy it's the &quot;antivirus&quot; of the Consensus, they're equiped with whatever they need to fulfil their role. If BSD were a notorious threath, they will be eradicated. As long as they aren't, it's a business for other people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason why the Technocracy doesn't go around doing this most of the time, is that they usually don't realize the threat involved. The &quot;good&quot; supernaturals keep themselves hidden well enough that they stay off the Union's hit list (even if they don't realize it), and frequently take out the &quot;bad&quot; supernaturals for the Technocracy anyway. As long as the fight between the Gaians and the BSDs doesn't break out into too much collateral damage into the mortal world, the Technocracy is happy to let them kill each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;irony&gt;Yeah, because the colateral damage caused by your average Traditional Chantry it's so much worse than what other supernaturals do every night. Yeah, totally believable&lt;/irony&gt;<br /> <br /> <i>In Werewolf there isn't a risk of being asaulted by armies of sci-fy stuff nor killed from the orbit if you break the veil.</i> If Technocracy was as strong in Werewolf as it's in Mage, they should be regarded as a threath on a level of magnitude equal or superior to that of DNA or Pentex First Teams (as far as hunters go. Like: you don't break the Veil, because the Weaver will send it's most potent minions if you do), instead of being regarded as a bizarre amalgamation of supernatural researchers that unwittingly serves the Weaver and rarely enters in contact with Garou (and, yeah, I know Technocracy doesn't care for spirits...but if you manage to get your terrorist mage captured in camera while he's &quot;in a mythical beast form with an aura of fear&quot;, I would think they would send someone to investigate)<br /> <br /> If the Wyrm was as active in Mage as it's in Werewolf...well, actually, you can have that because the only ones who <i>may </i>care are Void Engineers. Even VE have a hard time seeing the &quot;Spirit Wilds&quot; , and nobody listens to them anyway. Just keep the amount of mutants created by Pentex in a non-ludicrous level, and keep Dune worms inside the Middle Umbra most of the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-24-2017, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T09:13:59-07:00","id":1133408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133394#post1133394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Mage Technocracy it's the &quot;antivirus&quot; of the Consensus, they're equiped with whatever they need to fulfil their role. If BSD were a notorious threath, they will be eradicated. As long as they aren't, it's a business for other people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Other than the Pogrom against the Traditions, what else suggests this, and where is it written?<br /> To my mind comes Technocracy's attitude towards the Camarilla - non-interference. And I'm not swayed by possible counter-arguments that the Camarilla is somehow aligned to the Technocracy. In discrete ways, yes, but not in major ways - and especially not to the extent of Technocracy not being hostile to them for any other reason than the Technocracy's inability to effectively at least neutralize the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T09:20:05-07:00","id":1133413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133364#post1133364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it written anywhere when, how, and how often can the Technocracy do this (the nuking from the orbit part) ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really? But it's not exactly hard for them to do.<br /> <br /> Also keep in mind that there's a referential joke here to the movie Aliens (the mission is labelled a bug hunt during the initial briefing before the marines know what they're in for, and the survivors of the initial fight agree to nuke the place from orbit &quot;just to be sure&quot; rather than trying to fight the xenomorphs via infantry tactics).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133394#post1133394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Mage Technocracy it's the &quot;antivirus&quot; of the Consensus, they're equiped with whatever they need to fulfil their role.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really true. This is the role of Paradox (and esp. Paradox spirits). The Technocracy are a faction of mages with their own self-defined goals. They push to maintain the current state of Consensus because it aligns with their interests, not because Consensus demands it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &lt;irony&gt;Yeah, because the colateral damage caused by your average Traditional Chantry it's so much worse than what other supernaturals do every night. Yeah, totally believable&lt;/irony&gt; </div> </div> </div>Well, from a Mage perspective it's important because Tradition Chantries are a much greater risk towards the creation of Reality Zones than a vampire killing a human for blood. In the big picture war over the control of Consensus, the damage your average supernatural monster does is less of a problem than what Tradition mages can do if left unchecked.<br /> <br /> So yes, the overall blindness of the Union to threats like the Wyrm is a flaw for them, it's a completely understandable one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>In Werewolf there isn't a risk of being asaulted by armies of sci-fy stuff nor killed from the orbit if you break the veil.</i> </div> </div> </div>Sure there is. It doesn't even have to come from the Union. W20 has a DNA cybertech equivalent Weaver organization that creates Terminators to send after Garou, and governments with full modern military weaponry are aware of the existence of the supernatural who would certainly get hot with those weapons if you start breaking the veil too much.<br /> <br /> The fact that WtA doesn't even feel the need to have the Union step in to make these things threats says enough in my mind about how big of a threat they'd be.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T09:36:16-07:00","id":1133421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers#post1133232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Technocracy notices a Level 5 Pit and realizes the threat the BSDs pose to the locals, how likely is it that they will unleash an army of magitech wielding terminators on them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps you might come to better understand the Technocracy's attitude and possible approaches if you read this thread about a possible Technocracy Civil War, and think how each of the factions, detailed by CTPhipps, would act.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1122213-technocracy-civil-war-campaign-idea/page2\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ign-idea/page2</a><br /> The Throne, for example, would possibly form some understanding - or even an alliance - with the Princes of Ruin Black Spiral Dancer Tribal Camp.<br /> The Foundation would try to neutralize them first and foremost, using the challenge as a test bed for new technologies.<br /> Invictus would try to eliminate the Black Spiral Dancer Pit, but with the aim of keeping innocent casualties at a minimum. (How would they act in a possible hostage holding situation?)<br /> As you can probably see, there is more to the Technocracy than eliminating the opposition using maximum force.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133413#post1133413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really? But it's not exactly hard for them to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Where is this written/said?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 08-24-2017, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T10:11:19-07:00","id":1133433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers#post1133232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Technocracy notices a Level 5 Pit and realizes the threat the BSDs pose to the locals, how likely is it that they will unleash an army of magitech wielding terminators on them?</div> </div> </div> </div>The probability of using maximum firepower is a slight one I'd say - in my headcanon Technocracy can do so rarely and only against threats who are overt and/or investigated and properly identified over a relatively long period of time (HIT Marks and long-range weaponry have to be aimed and directed etc. et al.). Full force responses by the Technocracy also require specific Conventions and Methodologies to be present, active, and working together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T10:29:32-07:00","id":1133439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133393#post1133393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, then the other hives would probably enter high alert, particularly other Level 5 Pits, and they would find out who did it, giving the rest of the Technocracy a rather severe problem to deal with in the future, particularly in Russia, where the BSDs have Zmei on their side.<br /> <br /> However, Pentex vs. the Union? That's a no-contest victory for Pentex. You'd have a better time convincing the Union that all members should saw off their own feet than you would convincing them that Pentex's practices are a problem. The Union eats, breaths, and sleeps the kind of reckless economic raiding that Pentex represents. The Union as a whole is so blind to its faults that the other Conventions haven't noticed anything up with the Syndicate, and the Syndicate still thinks that there's something that they can salvage from their SPD clusterfuck. When it comes to operations, the TU always yields to the purse strings. It's the fundamental reality that they've accepted as their own, and they wouldn't be able to escape from it without completely abandoning their course for the past several centuries and starting over.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't imagine any scenario where Pentex still exists if the Technocracy could actually get off its' ass and do things. Garou can't do anything about high finance as it's beyond their mandate but the Technocracy controls the concept of money.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy is easily the group in the WOD *BEST EQUIPPED* to destroy it.<br /> <br /> And literally none of what you said about them above is true in current canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T12:42:06-07:00","id":1133506,"title":"","content":"Point of Order: Developmental Neogenetics Amalgamated does not use terminators. Shinzui Industries might.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133439#post1133439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't imagine any scenario where Pentex still exists if the Technocracy could actually get off its' ass and do things. Garou can't do anything about high finance as it's beyond their mandate but the Technocracy controls the concept of money.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, Garou could, but are driven not to because they haven't gotten around to adjusting to the world, at least by and large. That's the weak link - not that they could never communicate with spirits necessary to start clamping down on a major artery of their enemy, but that only one or two tribes really has.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Technocracy is easily the group in the WOD *BEST EQUIPPED* to destroy it. </div> </div> </div>Only if they like the idea of cutting off massive amounts of their own resources first. Which they probably don't want to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And literally none of what you said about them above is true in current canon. </div> </div> </div>Really? The Synidcate isn't scared that the other Conventions will find out about SPD and pull them apart? The Technocracy isn't based on scarcity and modern economic systems, right down to the importance that they, at least for the &quot;time being&quot;, grind some people down into the dirt while handing immense amounts of resources and privilege to a much smaller group? Because it seems like that's an incredibly large cornerstone of its plan, and Pentex, among other WICs, is wrapped around and all inside of it as among the richest of the privileged that the Technocracy wants to have around.<br /> <br /> The modern world is one the Technocracy wanted the most. And in a crossover with Werewolf, this makes them enablers of the highest order when it comes to WICs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T13:38:37-07:00","id":1133533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133408#post1133408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? Other than the Pogrom against the Traditions, what else suggests this, and where is it written?<br /> To my mind comes Technocracy's attitude towards the Camarilla - non-interference. And I'm not swayed by possible counter-arguments that the Camarilla is somehow aligned to the Technocracy. In discrete ways, yes, but not in major ways - and especially not to the extent of Technocracy not being hostile to them for any other reason than the Technocracy's inability to effectively at least neutralize the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's the Iteration X revised book where a single Hardsuited Iterator wipes out an entire vampire stronghold solo using hand to hand and a flamethrower. Also the part where they explain just how easy it is to find Vampires.<br /> <br /> It's not that they don't know. It's just that they don't care. Even the Iterators only care so far as it gives them an acceptable target to take their warmongering instincts out on in absence of a Pogrom to pursue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133506#post1133506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? The Synidcate isn't scared that the other Conventions will find out about SPD and pull them apart? The Technocracy isn't based on scarcity and modern economic systems, right down to the importance that they, at least for the &quot;time being&quot;, grind some people down into the dirt while handing immense amounts of resources and privilege to a much smaller group? Because it seems like that's an incredibly large cornerstone of its plan, and Pentex, among other WICs, is wrapped around and all inside of it as among the richest of the privileged that the Technocracy wants to have around.<br /> <br /> The modern world is one the Technocracy wanted the most. And in a crossover with Werewolf, this makes them enablers of the highest order when it comes to WICs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the modern world ISN'T the world the Technocracy wanted the most. The Modern world is a flawed stepping stone to the perfect world of Unity.<br /> <br /> And no, no the technocracy isn't based on Scarcity and modern economic systems. <i>Certain factions within the technocracy</i> are based on those things. All of the others use it as a tool. Iteration X doesn't give a damn about scarcity and have zero problems just materializing stuff out of thin air as long as they do it via science. They consider the Syndicate a convention of cowards and fools, who are tolerated only as an extra, non-essential source of energy to fuel the war effort, and once the Pogrom ended, so too did the syndicates sole justification for existence in the Eyes of Iteration X. The Progenitors play along with the syndicate because they have their biggest moneymaker by the throat, and don't mind shaking them down for some extra quintessence. The VE are reliant on the syndicate only insofar as they are currently the only convention on war footing. And thus, the only convention actually wanting quintessence. The NWO actively dislike the Syndicate and have had no problems backing planned economies in the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11744,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","user":"Enginseer-42","date":". 08-24-2017, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T13:45:28-07:00","id":1133536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133413#post1133413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not really true. This is the role of Paradox (and esp. Paradox spirits). The Technocracy are a faction of mages with their own self-defined goals. They push to maintain the current state of Consensus because it aligns with their interests, not because Consensus demands it.</div> </div> </div> </div>From a metaplot perspective, you're right, however, from a storytelling perspective the Technocracy it's what usually appears when your mages get too noisy but do not have heavy Paradox ratting. They do label what Traditionalists do as crimes against Reality and act as Consensus guardians.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, from a Mage perspective it's important because Tradition Chantries are a much greater risk towards the creation of Reality Zones than a vampire killing a human for blood. In the big picture war over the control of Consensus, the damage your average supernatural monster does is less of a problem than what Tradition mages can do if left unchecked.<br /> <br /> So yes, the overall blindness of the Union to threats like the Wyrm is a flaw for them, it's a completely understandable one. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you're right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure there is. It doesn't even have to come from the Union. W20 has a DNA cybertech equivalent Weaver organization that creates Terminators to send after Garou, and governments with full modern military weaponry are aware of the existence of the supernatural who would certainly get hot with those weapons if you start breaking the veil too much. </div> </div> </div>As SaurOps stated, this ain't so much the case. DNA hasn't crazy hypertech, only a few effective drugs and good tactics. DNA isn't as much a physical threath, their hunters can be dangerous, but not because they have&quot;super firepower&quot;.<br /> <br /> In general, the Technocracy doesn't figure as part of the multiple kinds of Hunters that will appear if a Garou breaks the Veil, but it's the first thing that happens when a mage does...trying to obfuscate that this happens because Werewolf and Mage are separate gamelines and mostly irrelevant to each other it's like trying to hide the sun with your finger.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The fact that WtA doesn't even feel the need to have the Union step in to make these things threats says enough in my mind about how big of a threat they'd be. </div> </div> </div>How so?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaurOps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? The Synidcate isn't scared that the other Conventions will find out about SPD and pull them apart? The Technocracy isn't based on scarcity and modern economic systems, right down to the importance that they, at least for the &quot;time being&quot;, grind some people down into the dirt while handing immense amounts of resources and privilege to a much smaller group? Because it seems like that's an incredibly large cornerstone of its plan, and Pentex, among other WICs, is wrapped around and all inside of it as among the richest of the privileged that the Technocracy wants to have around.<br /> <br /> The modern world is one the Technocracy wanted the most. And in a crossover with Werewolf, this makes them enablers of the highest order when it comes to WICs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, all of this it's true, however, that's not the reason of why Technocracy isn't going to fight Pentex. The reason it's, as Heavy Arms said, that the Technocracy refuses to understand the threat.<br /> Pentex threat it's mostly spiritual in it's nature, and the Technocracy as a whole doesn't care about that. Pentex doesn't state that their goal it's the destruction of the planet, it just happens that they help to empower a massive spiritual force that's going to do that. Pentex actually produces quality tech, generates quality jobs, produces wealth (and probably donates to charity or some other bullshit). What's so wrong with them?<br /> Sure, they're infested by EDE, but who isn't?, there's EDE everywhere. Sure they contaminate and conduct less than legitimate business, when we fix every other problem in the world we will fix them. SPD nephandic corruption (among other &quot;deviants&quot; that are present in it's power structure) it's the only thing they can't completely ignore, that's why the secret Project Invictus exists, to root out the Nephandi that are <i>corrupting Pentex </i>(jejeje).<br /> <br /> If the Technocracy were to believe Pentex it's as dangerous as Garou and Dreamspeakers say it is, they would do the impossible to break it's power, including allying with the Traditions and helping Garou. This ain't going to be the case. Unless Pentex starts spawing hordes of monsters, they aren't a danger to the modern world, or that's what Technocracy believes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-24-2017, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T13:55:52-07:00","id":1133539,"title":"","content":"As of the Syndicate Convention book, the Special Projects Division is GONE. Presumably because Pentex's masters ate them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T13:57:01-07:00","id":1133541,"title":"","content":"I see the Technocracy as having a grand strategy, and what they do is based on operations that fit that strategy. They don't deviate from it unless a large enough threat develops that they must deal with it.<br /> <br /> So that level 5 Pit is ignored unless it starts threatening critical things like overall belief in the supernatural or an important asset. They rely on the normal opponents of their enemies to deal with that. So if a level 5 Pit gets frisky with the locals, they might arrange for some information to be handed over to Gaian Garou surreptitiously so they can be dealt with if it doesn't look like the Garou are already planning on doing something about it.<br /> <br /> But if the threat level increases and the foe's natural enemies can't handle it, then the Technocracy eliminates the threat. But that always come at a cost as they lose resources, assets, and delay other operations as a result.<br /> <br /> I see the Technocracy as being very powerful, but most of their power is used in only two things. The first is maintaining what they already have and protecting it from attack. The second are reserves saved for truly awful and unexpected threats like Nephandi raising Cthulhu. In terms of what is available for offense, it is limited and is deployed according to plans already made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T14:56:38-07:00","id":1133561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133421#post1133421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? Where is this written/said?</div> </div> </div> </div>GttTech, the Conventionbooks, logical extrapolation of what some of the 6+ Backgrounds the Technocrats can get in M20 (or just the Requisition Background in general).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133433#post1133433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Full force responses by the Technocracy also require specific Conventions and Methodologies to be present, active, and working together.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is, however I think a problem with this conversation.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy's ability to act in unison is their greatest strength. Despite their internal power struggles, brewing internal civil war, and all that, when they are confronted by a major threat, they can become the Monolith. They aren't a confederation of disparate groups forced to work together like the Traditions. They aren't divided into a cell style structure like the Garou where most local areas are independent from each other. The Union is (since the Victorian restructuring) is a single global organization with parts designed to work together where ever they're needed. The Technocracy can call down power like few other WoD groups because they're designed to do exactly that: being maximum power to bear as fast as possible to eliminate threats as effectively as possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133506#post1133506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point of Order: Developmental Neogenetics Amalgamated does not use terminators. Shinzui Industries might.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133536#post1133536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As SaurOps stated, this ain't so much the case. DNA hasn't crazy hypertech, only a few effective drugs and good tactics. DNA isn't as much a physical threath, their hunters can be dangerous, but not because they have&quot;super firepower&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, you both seem to have misread what I wrote.<br /> <br /> Please refer to CyberSolutions in W20, which does, in fact, make cyborg soldiers specifically designed to pass as normal humans to sneak high end military weaponry into enemy territory (aka Terminators).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From a metaplot perspective, you're right, however, from a storytelling perspective the Technocracy it's what usually appears when your mages get too noisy but do not have heavy Paradox ratting. They do label what Traditionalists do as crimes against Reality and act as Consensus guardians. </div> </div> </div>Unless you're running a Technocracy game...<br /> <br /> Also they label the Garou Reality Deviants too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How so? </div> </div> </div>If things like CyberSolutions and SAD are meant to be effective antagonists for WtA, the Technocracy are those taken to 11.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T00:46:02-07:00","id":1133697,"title":"","content":"It really depends on the situation, the setting you are playing and the threat level. <br /> <br /> If the situation really gets dangerous for fellow conventions, innocent humans, and the bsd start to rape kill or kidnap children and innocent women to breed new kinfolk, then the tech will probably enter the scene, otherwise it won't intervene. <br /> <br /> Are we talking about what technocrats REALLY can do in an actual wod realistic setting? <br /> Well.... Things don't actually look so good for the bsd pit. <br /> <br /> First, we need to think that the technocrats capacity for heavy weaponry really depends on the local assets, resources and time. <br /> <br /> If they simply don't have enough men, money or amalgams to deal with the situation, they would try at least to contain the danger hunting lonely packs from distance, quietly damaging spirits in the umbra with procedures, and generally blocking the werewolves before they can harm the local human population. <br /> <br /> Another favorite tactic is simply passing the information about the pit to the right supernaturals, like other groups of garou or hunters. <br /> <br /> Are we talking about a really serious and undeniable threat that even the nwo and syndicate cannot ignore? <br /> <br /> Well then, the first thing to do would be simply spying and reconnaissance. And the technocrats are very well prepared for that. <br /> <br /> Nwo cameras, microphones, cyber control, invisible and silent drones, access to phones and databases, server of security cameras and most importantly data, correspondence, time and entropy procedures, mean that they can access to any information they deem necessary. Names, social security numbers addresses of kinfolk and allies or relatives of the bsd will all be under strict surveillance. <br /> <br /> This also means that they would learn about bsd movements, sentinels and warding tactics. <br /> <br /> Correspondence and entropy procedures, coupled with matter and forces, mean that their surveillance would be very very very hard to find, even for bsd gifts. Unless the pit has access to very powerful mystic spritis, theurges that can detect magic and pierce other powers and use that power all the time , they won't notice the technocrats until it's too late. <br /> <br /> Correspondence allows the nwo to spy from distance not risking any casualty. Entropy means shit tons of extra dices or increasing the difficulty for enemies to spot the scrying. <br /> <br /> <br /> This is just the first half of the surveillance, the other half would be the study of the umbra and the wyrm servants that guard the caern. This would of course be a job for the void engineers. Their dimensional science coupled with correspondence mean that they would be able to spy on spirits and the pit umbral architecture from distance. Spirit (dimensional science) will also allow them to understand the spirits basic influences, powers and rank and determine the threat level. <br /> <br /> Now, comes the actual planning for extermination. <br /> If, and only if_ syndicate fully found such a dangerous mission, supplying every amalgam with weaponry and assets, IF the nwo deems the extermination absolutely necessary and If and only if there are enough resources, men and advantages involved, then they would attack. <br /> <br /> I strongly put emphasis on the if factor because otherwise they would not simply act foolishly like some white howler with suicidal tendencies. Technocrats only attack when that really need to, and most importantly only when they think they can reasonbly win by any means. <br /> <br /> Now, one thing that that almost everyone ignores about technocrats and procedures. <br /> <br /> THEY HAVE TIME and ENTROPY procedures. <br /> <br /> What does this means? Simply put, they will almost certainly have the strategic and time advantage. Nwo agents and syndicate statisticians will calculate every risk, every possibility and every possible development of the assault. Nwo virtual simulators and quantum computers, coupled with syndicate entropy flow will allow the assault team to carefully plan the attack, value the overall risk and how many casualties will it probably cost. This isn't a factor we should put out of the picture, because it means that simply put, unless werewolves have access to powerful time spirits, mages will have the overwhelming strategic advantage in a war. Period. <br /> <br /> Now, with all things said, let's see how a similar attack scenario would play out. <br /> <br /> First off, why would the union risk losing men and useful amalgams under bsd fangs when they can simply attack from distance? <br /> <br /> Here's how an actual full force union assault would play out. <br /> On this side of the gauntlet, they probably won't even use that much enlightened agents or special ops. It's stupid and will only cause useless bloodshed and casualties. <br /> <br /> Why not employ hit marks, cyborgs and drones? <br /> Honestly, do u guys have any idea what a terryfing sight would be for the bsd to witness weird flying objects 50 or 60 meters in the air that can full auto shoot them with silver bullets? <br /> <br /> Not only would drones be employed, but snipers too. People seems to forget how modern warfare look like. Picture something like &quot;death from above&quot; and &quot;oh shit wtf we are dead&quot; <br /> Technocrats snipers armed with hypertech Barret 50 caliber enhanced with matter and forces and entropy procedures will surely headshot any wolf on sight. This, coupled with time and entropy procedures, simulations and careful study of the area will give them the utmost certainty thy they will hit, and hit HARD. <br /> A regular , not awakened sniper rifle can hit from pretty afar. <br /> Maximum Range7,450 yd (6,812 m)<br /> Maximum Effective Range2,000 yd (1,829 m<br /> These are the numbers for a Barrett in the real world, and we can safely assume that an enhanced version would be even more powerful. <br /> The bottom line is THE DANCERS WON'T EVEN KNOW WHAT HIT THEM&quot;. <br /> <br /> {end of part 1)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T00:50:46-07:00","id":1133699,"title":"","content":"(part 2}<br /> <br /> Let's not forget about another practical mean of war. Explosions. Let's talk about the big guns. <br /> Are we facing werewolves? Well, how about silver sharpnel bombs argued with matter and forces procedures? <br /> I'm assuming since we are talking about a level 5 pit caern that either :<br /> 1_ we are talking about a very isolated rural caern<br /> 2_ the caern is a hidden urban caern probably in the worst part of the worst criminal ridden city<br /> 3_the caern is in the umbra<br /> <br /> This means the nwo can go full monkey crazy on the &quot;hiding the masses&quot; thing, and can probably employ high potency explosions filled with silver, poison gas (I guess it won't be that hard for iteration x to come up with a toxic gas that can kill even a garou), rocket launchers and cannons. <br /> <br /> Up until now, we took a look on the &quot; kill them from distance&quot; approach. But this doesn't mean techno won't get their hands dirty if necessary. <br /> <br /> After the first bombing and full force artillery assault, hit marks and cyborgs will close in. <br /> They will probably be enhanced with extra procedures and equipment but surely enough each one of them will be armed with a full auto heavy machine gun or assault rifle, possibly loaded with high enhanced silver bullets. <br /> <br /> Still, maybe bombing and silver bullets won't be enough. That's when, only if it's really necessary, will the other spec ops and agents intervene. <br /> <br /> Progenitors, enforcers of the syndicate and nwo special operations agents will probably take the lead here possibly escorted by void engineers neutralization corps. <br /> <br /> They will of course be equipped with the best weapons , matter and life procedures for extra armor, extra health, and capability to absorb aggravated damage, also dimensional science procedures to interfere with werewolves gifts and powers. Silver bullets and heavy weapons are the minimum requirement of course, possibly enhanced with forces for extra bullet damage, and flashbombs and granades capable of stunning or wounding garous. <br /> <br /> Let's not forget entropy and time procedures simulations to have the maximum effect (technically speaking, extra dices to attack, dodge and damage their opponents or win the initiative). <br /> <br /> _ doesn't really look good for the bsd pit right? <br /> <br /> But aren't we forgetting something? <br /> In the midst of the heavy fire, fomori and kinfolk are chopped to pieces like cardboards, silver sharpnels wound the pack mates, and full auto fire from Silver bullets machine guns is killing werewolves from above and from every directions, snipers and hit marks seem to never run out of ammo (and actually they do, and don't even need to reload, thanks to matter and correspondence procedures..) <br /> <br /> But theurges and other alphas smile. They have allies and powers that these fools don't even imagine. They are ready to call upon the forces of the wyrm, unleash the dark servants, banes, and guardians from the other side of the gauntlet. They might even try to call a nexus crawler or let the totem of the caern himself join them in the battle. They start the rituals and gifts to evoke the spirits and.... Nothing happen. No one answers, and they only get confusing signals from the gauntlet. What happened? <br /> <br /> It's simple. Void engineers are doing their job. <br /> <br /> Now, void engineers have two ways of hindering and weakening the pit:<br /> <br /> 1_ strengthen the gauntlet and prevent spirits or spirit influences to reach the other side of reality, blocking spirit powers and interfering with sidestepping and theurges rituals<br /> <br /> 2_straight up murdering and assaulting the spirit population of the caern with heavy plasma weapons and bombs. <br /> <br /> Bad news for bsd is that they can and probably will do both things. <br /> <br /> Void engineers shuttles and heavy armed teams will close in on the caern shooting the totem and every spiritual being in range with plasma cannons, rockets and dimensional bombs ready for the occasion, courtesy of the iteration x heavy weaponry department. They will probably accumulate enough successes to inflict at least 15+automatic agg damage with each dimensional bomb, and they will use a lot of them. <br /> <br /> Let's not forget that since they are in the umbra, THERE WILL BE NO PARADOX INVOLVED. so basically the union and void can and will go full dragon ball Z on their enemies. <br /> <br /> Full armored enhanced Alanson and Martinez suit armor with plasma cannon arete 6 forces agg damage, armor with 8 dices to soak agg damage, extra health and bonus to stamina, automatic firing systems, and life auto regenerating suits that heal their wounds. Yep. <br /> They will probably engage only after the firing from distance and dimensional bombing are finished., to finish off any entity still alive. <br /> <br /> Also, unless spirits can fly or have access to blast charms or powers that work from distance, they will never actually engage them in a melee fight, they will be shooting them from afar, and never allow them to get close (shoot and cover tactics). <br /> Alanson armors can fly, and can be pretty fast too. <br /> <br /> The void approach will be very simple with the caern imbalance and population in the umbra &quot;NUKE THEM ALL&quot; and move on, not kidding here they are very well equipped and honestly won't even engage the enemy at close range. They will start blasting them with dimensional bombs and plasma cannons from very far, resorting to Alanson full suits if the enemy get close. <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, the assault doesn't look good for the bsd IF the technocrats have the time and entropy advantage, numbers and resources necessary. This in my mind is how it would play out, if the union has all the time and preparation necessary. <br /> <br /> Keep in mind that this is all theory, not actual game play, and maybe in reality things would payout differently. We are not counting possible allies, influences and powers on each side (what if the bsd have some nephandi at the caern? What if the union allies with glass walkers and hunters? What if vampires and real government will be involved? Etc.. Etc... ) <br /> <br /> But this is, at least POTENTIALLY what the union might do if really forces to intervene with extreme measures. So to sum it up :<br /> <br /> On this side of the gauntlet :<br /> 1_ drones and bombs, rockets and snipers start shooting every wolf or fomori in sight, killing lot of bsd or at least wounding them to the point of frenzy, chaos and mayhem and death roam free in the pit. Everything enhanced with forces matter and silver loaded. <br /> <br /> 2_ cyborg hit marks with silver ammo charge and approach the remaining enemies, full auto shooting them. <br /> <br /> 3_if necessary, spec ops enforcers, agents and Progenitors will engage the remaining enemies who hiding or using gifts, provided with extra procedures and equipment to face werewolves in a fight. <br /> <br /> On the other side of the gauntlet <br /> <br /> 1_ void engineers will hinder the influence of the spirits and wyrm totems, interfering with their powers and the ability of side stepping of both spirits and werewolves <br /> <br /> 2_they will nuke the pit from above with rockets, plasma cannons and dimensional bombs killing the weaker banes and weakening the strongest spirits, and then will engage only if necessary with Alanson ed suits plasma cannons and enhanced spec ops. <br /> <br /> <br /> Hope this makes sense it took me a lot to write this down on my phone lol. Again, this is all on paper, in an actual game it really depends on how strong the technocracy or the werewolves are in your game. And most importantly, if the game u are playing its called mage the ascension or werewolf the apocalypse. <br /> <br /> Ps_ lot of things written here come from my crossover experience of werewolf and mage, a crazy chronicle where mages and wolves were forced to collaborate to defeat the Deceiver head of the wyrm before the apocalypse. <br /> <br /> Pps,,,_ I didn't mention it but of course drones and hit marks will be equipped with night vision and heat vision system, infrared sensors and so on... So yeah no cover and no hiding. <br /> In my personal experience , a nephandi sniper with correspondence and matter can easily kill even a rank 4 werewolf. Actually happened during a session. <br /> <br /> Pppps....yeah.. Forgot about mind procedures... If nwo is able to capture a kinfolk a fomori or a young bad pup the they can simply scan his mind to learn everything about the caern.. Then reprogram him and have an inside spy or assassin at the right moment...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T07:10:20-07:00","id":1133774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lasombra</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Void engineers shuttles and heavy armed teams will close in on the caern shooting the totem and every spiritual being in range with plasma cannons, rockets and dimensional bombs ready for the occasion, courtesy of the iteration x heavy weaponry department. They will probably accumulate enough successes to inflict at least 15+automatic agg damage with each dimensional bomb, and they will use a lot of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>15+ Aggravated? Don't sell VE that short <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> , that's standard voisdship armament, they surely have greater stuff for those nastiness that's above mere Nexus Crawlers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I mostly agree on the tactics, though, albeit most of your post assumes the unlikely case that the Technocracy decides to go full Code Ragnarok on them.<br /> <br /> I think we mostly need to focus on the idea that the Technocracy isn't going to spend a good chunk of it's resouces on this. They don't do so in Mexico City, with all the supernatural killing 'n rapping that happens there, they will hardly do so in this situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HeavyArms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you're running a Technocracy game...</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, they have laws against causing paradox, thus, in a sense, you can be prevented from going full gonzo with the Spheres in earthpace by the Technocracy even while playing with them. As a narrative tool, they're good at this, arguably better than Paradox depending on how you interpret the rules, how many anti Paradox resources your players have, and much &quot;by the rules&quot; you play.<br /> <br /> But, from a strict Lore perspective, you're totally right, Technocrats are &quot;reality deviants&quot; too, even if they deny it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also they label the Garou Reality Deviants too. </div> </div> </div>And this is why, in a believable crossover universe, Garou, vampires and the rest should be much more conscious of them than what they are. For instance, vampires shouldn't ignore them as a danger to building blood cults, because that does generate Reality Zones. Garou should have them as a cautionary tale about breaking the veil, and they should know them by name because if any mage faction it's capable of stealing and sanitizing their precious Caerns, it's the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">If things like CyberSolutions and SAD are meant to be effective antagonists for WtA, the Technocracy are those taken to 11.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I like this argument, let's call it &quot;the power scaling argument&quot;: Technocracy &gt; CyberSolutions. If the latter was a problem, woe if you ever encounter the former.<br /> <br /> I don't know how dangerous are those two when compared to the average threath Garou face, though. In Werewolf you hear a lot about Pentex but the SAD it's mentioned as a small compact of weirdos, that do evil research, some of which are mages, they do not seem to be the scariest nor the most powerful branch of Pentex. No one says: careful about messing with Pentex, the SAD it's going to get you if you do. It's </span>CyberSolutions depicted as a serious danger?<br /> <br /> Anycase, all the more reason to believe that the Technocracy it's weaker in Werewolf, because otherwise they would be known as more than an odd group composed mostly of researchers (last time I read the Book of the Weaver, they sounded very unintimidating. Even DNA seems more intimidating than the technocracy in that book, and they're explicitly not a physical threath-as in, their agents have no chance against a werewolf unless they take it by surprise. I'm not saying that this make sense, I think it doesn't).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T08:38:08-07:00","id":1133801,"title":"","content":"See, I don't think boots would hit the ground at all.<br /> <br /> They'd just park a ship loaded with Neutron pattern disruptors in geosynchronous orbit and bsd's would just start bleeding out of their everything before falling over dead. Killed by invisible space rays that pass through solid objects.<br /> <br /> Things would be mildly more exciting in the Umbra, where the attack would be opened up with spirit bans to prevent crossing the Umbra followed by saturation bombardment on the umbra side to kill off any EDE threats.<br /> <br /> To everyone else it would be a perfectly normal day. This could happen in a city center and go entirely unnoticed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T08:45:43-07:00","id":1133805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133774#post1133774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 15+ Aggravated? Don't sell VE that short <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> , that's standard voisdship armament, they surely have greater stuff for those nastiness that's above mere Nexus Crawlers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I mostly agree on the tactics, though, albeit most of your post assumes the unlikely case that the Technocracy decides to go full Code Ragnarok on them.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol i agree, and of course i was downplaying the iterators and engineers here... If they really put their machines to work, they can easily build bombs and weapons wth enough successes to inflict at least 25+ aggravated damage every turn, so yeah even a nexus crawler will have a very hard time substain a dimensional bombing like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133774#post1133774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I mostly agree on the tactics, though, albeit most of your post assumes the unlikely case that the Technocracy decides to go full Code Ragnarok on them.<br /> <br /> I think we mostly need to focus on the idea that the Technocracy isn't going to spend a good chunk of it's resouces on this. They don't do so in Mexico City, with all the supernatural killing 'n rapping that happens there, they will hardly do so in this situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely agree, and it won't probably happen in a real game unless the bsd were specifically targeting agents or amalgams... but still, we are really pushing the edges here and i was trying to give a complete analysis for the OP <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T08:47:18-07:00","id":1133809,"title":"","content":"Little appendix and side note regarding spirits, umbra and other factors in play. <br /> <br /> Void engineers and agents will never ever ever ever engage in a melee or brawl battle with spirits or werewolves if possible. Think about marine troops and spec ops if they had to deal with a giant bear or dangerous subject that can outmatch them with brute strength. Do u think they will attack him with a knife or shoot him from 200 meters? <br /> <br /> Thus is the bottom line, always think that what happens in the handbook illustrations (technocrats fighting toe to toe with vampires and monsters) won't probably happen in a &quot;real&quot; fight, and snipers and flying agents will be employed. Arhoun and spirits who can't access to long distance attack, charms or gifts are pretty much screwed, and won't even be able to touch or wound the mages.<br /> <br /> Even when blast charms or gifts are employed, or mind influence , consider this :<br /> <br /> 1_ dimensional Science can block or defend mages against spirit powers and bad gifts<br /> 2_mind procedures can shield from mind control and influence <br /> <br /> <br /> Another thing to establish is if orbital cannons are out of service or not. In the post anomaly setting, most of void engineers forces were killed or maimed and they lost their most powerful weapon , laser cannon that can shoot from space. My analysis focus on this post anomaly world. If the technology is still as in pre anomaly union, then they can simply disintegrate the entire caern from space. <br /> <br /> Now, on the black spiral defense :<br /> <br /> Worst thing that amalgams and agents can face is simply bad technology jam. This could happen in two ways:<br /> <br /> 1_ gifts that can shut down or hinder technology(looking at u, jam technology) <br /> 2_ rites that ward against weapons and hypertech<br /> <br /> If the union doesn't foresee this event, then they are pretty much fucked. They will simple lose a lot of weapons, hypertech and resources. <br /> However, if they employ entropy and time procedures, they will see during the simulation that wolf magic and spirits can pretty much fuck up their equipment and shut everything off if they get too close. <br /> <br /> The solution? <br /> Simply never approach at closers range the enemy. Shoot from above. Shoot them from distance. <br /> <br /> Jam technology is very good at stopping cyborgs and heavy machine guns, but only if u can see them. When I'm shooting u heavy caliber or bombs from 300 ft in the air, and my drones and snipers are basically invisible ( forces and matter procedures) then all the warding and gifts won't save you. Ward against technology won't stop my heavy silver bullet from piercing your skull from 1km away. <br /> <br /> If this is not possible , void engineers and iteration X will probably come up with a mixed procedure of matter spirit and something else to counter those gifts effects. <br /> <br /> Another thing people tend to forget... Mage and technocrats can also employ wards and barriers... <br /> Procedures involving correspondence, dimensional science and possibly prime batteries can create effective wards against other powers specifically wolf gifts and spirit charms, and can definitely block their attack before it reach the agents. <br /> <br /> <br /> Again, all of this is pure speculation. <br /> <br /> If the pit know about the attack and they can prepare an ambush, then the battle won't go as well as the union might plan. <br /> If they employ wyrm magic, powerful rites or ancient horrors evoked by nephandi magic... Then everything will go ballistic and who knows who might win the race here... <br /> <br /> <br /> But given time and preparation and especially if the union employs his Time and Entropy proecedures, then the pit will fall without even realizing they were under attack. <br /> Imho","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T08:56:27-07:00","id":1133812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lasombra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133697#post1133697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It<br /> <br /> Why not employ hit marks, cyborgs and drones?<br /> Honestly, do u guys have any idea what a terryfing sight would be for the bsd to witness weird flying objects 50 or 60 meters in the air that can full auto shoot them with silver bullets?</div> </div> </div> </div>The majority wouldn't be. Hrugglings or similar air-controlling banes would end up fouling the airborne view of the battlefield and also likely the engines. Dancers are also likely capable of conjuring up hurricane-force storms, just like every other type of monster is. One corrupted Shadow Lord's experimental rite later, and a sudden thunderstorm that's crept into the stratosphere sends everything up in the air to the ground in a mass incidence of deconstructive lithobraking, and hits them with cloud to ground lightning, just to be sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not only would drones be employed, but snipers too. People seems to forget how modern warfare look like. Picture something like &quot;death from above&quot; and &quot;oh shit wtf we are dead&quot;<br /> Technocrats snipers armed with hypertech Barret 50 caliber enhanced with matter and forces and entropy procedures will surely headshot any wolf on sight. This, coupled with time and entropy procedures, simulations and careful study of the area will give them the utmost certainty thy they will hit, and hit HARD.<br /> A regular , not awakened sniper rifle can hit from pretty afar.<br /> Maximum Range7,450 yd (6,812 m)<br /> Maximum Effective Range2,000 yd (1,829 m<br /> These are the numbers for a Barrett in the real world, and we can safely assume that an enhanced version would be even more powerful.<br /> The bottom line is THE DANCERS WON'T EVEN KNOW WHAT HIT THEM&quot;.<br /> <br /> {end of part 1) </div> </div> </div>A pit is subterranean. Snipers will be of limited use when the scenario is an awful lot of blind fire in tunnels. That's why I have to go with Heavy Arms on how the Union would actually handle it; they don't want to worry about &quot;Jesus Christ Apone, what's going on?&quot; or &quot;GAME OVER, MAN!&quot; So they won't, and will send in explosions instead of thinning out their ranks of agents. To the extent that explosions can help with a dug-in position like a subterranean pit that has a caern totem-level bane backing it up.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, however, it's both subterranean and mobile, such as the Trinity Hive. Grammaw can just move along deep in the earth to avoid air assaults, burrowing through rock with a superheated head, and travel to whatever Technocracy node is nearby, so as to eat it. It is not the only Organism-type pit, either, though it's inadvisable to try nuking it. It was a nuclear bomb that triggered the genesis of Thunderwyrms in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T09:37:32-07:00","id":1133831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133812#post1133812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The majority wouldn't be. Hrugglings or similar air-controlling banes would end up fouling the airborne view of the battlefield and also likely the engines. Dancers are also likely capable of conjuring up hurricane-force storms, just like every other type of monster is. One corrupted Shadow Lord's experimental rite later, and a sudden thunderstorm that's crept into the stratosphere sends everything up in the air to the ground in a mass incidence of deconstructive lithobraking, and hits them with cloud to ground lightning, just to be sure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A pit is subterranean. Snipers will be of limited use when the scenario is an awful lot of blind fire in tunnels. That's why I have to go with Heavy Arms on how the Union would actually handle it; they don't want to worry about &amp;quot;Jesus Christ Apone, what's going on?&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;GAME OVER, MAN!&amp;quot; So they won't, and will send in explosions instead of thinning out their ranks of agents. To the extent that explosions can help with a dug-in position like a subterranean pit that has a caern totem-level bane backing it up.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, however, it's both subterranean and mobile, such as the Trinity Hive. Grammaw can just move along deep in the earth to avoid air assaults, burrowing through rock with a superheated head, and travel to whatever Technocracy node is nearby, so as to eat it. It is not the only Organism-type pit, either, though it's inadvisable to try nuking it. It was a nuclear bomb that triggered the genesis of Thunderwyrms in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being underground doesn't provide protection from a npd. And Grammaw is more a liability than an asset, given she's just as vulnerable to being murdered as they are.<br /> <br /> Also space. Thunderstorms don't happen in space because there isn't any air.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, and it's rather cheesy, but format space. Static reality now works the way the union says it does within the borders of the hive. Meaning spirit gifts and rites no longer exist, your moon bridge just collapsed and you're stuck inside the rotting carcass of a thunderwyrm with Technocratic dimensional barriers keeping you in. Have fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T09:53:55-07:00","id":1133838,"title":"","content":"Most perceived problems of crossover come because one assumes that *my* magical thing it's going to be super effective just because nothing says it won't. Ignoring that the material most likely wasn't written with every gameline and every situation in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T09:54:42-07:00","id":1133839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133812#post1133812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The majority wouldn't be. Hrugglings or similar air-controlling banes would end up fouling the airborne view of the battlefield and also likely the engines. Dancers are also likely capable of conjuring up hurricane-force storms, just like ever