Cleaner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T10:37:27-07:00","id":1133852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lasombra</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Totally agree, one small example is that i simply forgot about underground tunnels and pits... i was simply focusing on the mage setting and forgetting everything about werewolf universe <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I was reffering more to Enginseer-42's continued (and unsustained) claim that the Ascencion War can be won and all the supernatural creatures of Earth instantly killed without any defense with just 80 or so successes from Format Reality, because a technocracy book says something that, with a VERY generous interpretation and blatant disregard of 99% of the fluff from Mage that makes other supernaturals a serious business, can be tortured to infer something along those lines. I'm willing to bet money that the authors weren't trying to make the Technocratic goal of purging Reality Deviants an 80 successes ritual.<br /> <br /> Or his inhability to see that a Thunderwyrm or similar creatures born on damage, bad vives, and nuclear furnaces may just be able to offer protection from &quot;neutron pattern disruptors&quot; magick....just because the artifact says it bypases all resistence, doesn't mean it can be aplied to a magical creature of fundamental entropy as easily as it would cut trough a bunker.<br /> <br /> In comparison, I find your convictions about the supremacy of the Technocracy entirely innocent and perfectly understandable. Mind you, I think you're right in thinking that spirit usage from BSD can be countered by Technocratical Procedures. And thinking that Thunderwyrm it's capable of resisting any kind of damage coming that sci-fy StarTreck technology bombs could produce it's also a conceit, to some extent (cute in comparison with Enginseer-42 overidealizations, but still...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-25-2017, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T11:10:27-07:00","id":1133867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133852#post1133852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was reffering more to Enginseer-42's continued (and unsustained) claim that the Ascencion War can be won and all the supernatural creatures of Earth instantly killed without any defense with just 80 or so successes from Format Reality, because a technocracy book says something that, with a VERY generous interpretation and blatant disregard of 99% of the fluff from Mage that makes other supernaturals a serious business, can be tortured to infer something along those lines. I'm willing to bet money that the authors weren't trying to make the Technocratic goal of purging Reality Deviants an 80 successes ritual.<br /> <br /> Or his inhability to see that a Thunderwyrm or similar creatures born on damage, bad vives, and nuclear furnaces may just be able to offer protection from &amp;quot;neutron pattern disruptors&amp;quot; magick....just because the artifact says it bypases all resistence, doesn't mean it can be aplied to a magical creature of fundamental entropy as easily as it would cut trough a bunker.<br /> <br /> In comparison, I find your convictions about the supremacy of the Technocracy entirely innocent and perfectly understandable. Mind you, I think you're right in thinking that spirit usage from BSD can be countered by Technocratical Procedures. And thinking that Thunderwyrm it's capable of resisting any kind of damage coming that sci-fy StarTreck technology bombs could produce it's also a conceit, to some extent (cute in comparison with Enginseer-42 overidealizations, but still...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it really? It says it alters the fundamental structure of reality. From there it's obvious that powers that don't exist in that model won't exist in that area.<br /> <br /> You've actually done a fairly good job persuading me as to why this would not work on a planetary scale, but a hive is a planet not.<br /> <br /> Then you simply unmake the thunderwyrm. It either exists and has a pattern that can be destroyed or does not. In which case it doesn't exist. Even if it's pattern is born of nasty as hell resonance, the targets resonance generally does not apply to effects.<br /> <br /> The problem is threefold.<br /> <br /> One the mage system was built to simulate cinematic urban fantasy. When applied on an industrial scale with an eye for efficiency and pragmatism rather than rule of cool it quite swiftly cracks the setting over it's knee.<br /> <br /> There is a faction that explicitly does this.<br /> <br /> And pitting the forces of the wyrm against mages completely destroys the very story niche the wyrm is meant to inhabit. Entropy is not absolute in mage. The world isn't spiralling to some pre destined end. There is no future but the ones mankind makes for themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T11:23:29-07:00","id":1133876,"title":"","content":"well, to clarify, i'm not saying that technocrats would always come out of this fight as winners or will necessarily wipe out any foe on sight.<br /> <br /> I think most likely they won't even try a full on assault like this and will resort to more evasive and &quot;ninja wise&quot; Tactics, like following lonley packs tracking them down and kill them one by one, i was simply trying to think about what would happen if the union really had to go for it and wipe out an entire enemy caern.<br /> <br /> I think that given time and preparation, and especially Time and Entropy as procedures and strategical advantage they would probably win and outmatch any power or strategy the bsd could pull out.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER- If things got out of hand, and they find the caern fully prepared and ready for battle.. that's entirely another story.<br /> if say, by any chance, the wyrm or his powerful totems decide to intervene and grant prophetic visions to the galliards of the tribe, or if they have spies or nephandi allies infiltrated in any o the conventions involved, then the scenario would seriously change and probably turn into a disaster for the union, lots and lots of casualties and possibly defeat.<br /> <br /> i think the main point here is prep time and strategic advantage... to create the perfect ambush.<br /> <br /> -If the mages and union have the upper hand, and they attack the caern by surprise, then the bsd are fucked.<br /> <br /> - if by any chance the bsd are aware of the assault even less than an hour before the actual attack, the union will encounter serious resistance and might not even be able to win the fight or they will suffer lot of casualties, and their best resort is attack from distance, bomb, and retreat.<br /> <br /> -if by any chance the bsd pit is fully aware of the incoming attack hours or days before, and even worst they have nephandi allies and powerful spirits on their side... well then somebody will probably have a hard time explaining to the technocratic board how the heck an entire army of cyborgs, scientists and special corps simply disappeared without trace... SPD would be like child's play in comparison...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Given that visions and prophecy are part of werewolf but they seldom appear as a constant and clear way to foresee the future, and given that on the contrary mages use time and entropy rotes or procedures all the time to prepare for a fight, i tend however to be more on the union side, just because Time, Correspondence and Entropy and prep time give them an undeniable advantage on the battlefield.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T14:11:03-07:00","id":1133942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Does it really? <b>It says it alters the fundamental structure of reality</b>. From there it's obvious that powers that don't exist in that model won't exist in that area.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Magick does that. When you put that rote within the perspective of other books, what does this actually </span><i><b>means</b></i><span style=\"font-size:13px\">?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Consider this:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">A Horizon Realm it's a place where Reality(tm) it's defined by the mage who builds it. All the magick of the mage or mages Paradigm it's Coincident (hence why they a good place to live eternaly) and, conviniently, all the magick that isn't part of the Realm's Paradigm becomes Vulgar, which it's a good protection from invading forces. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Reality inside a Horizon Realm it's usualy of a similar nature as that of Eath (there's solid matter, organic life, natural forces) because mages usualy like to have a body and &quot;feel like home&quot;.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Horizon Realms can be inhabited by creatures appropiate to the local Paradigm, and Traditionalists use them as home of mythical beasts now that Earth has become way to techocratical for them to live there without becoming thaumnivores nor spirits. Being in the realm helps with that. What is never stated it's if the creatures inside that space that do not bend to the local Paradigm die out. Then again, you usually do not build a Realm with the intent to kill al nearby lifeforms </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">A Horizon Realm it's </span><span style=\"font-size:13px\">surrounded </span><span style=\"font-size:13px\">by a Pericarp, that can easily be of level 10, if the mage it's paranoid about incursions. this is why these realms are usually accessed by portals. Interestingly, </span><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Pericarp it's a key word in mage that's employed to define the outer layers of a realm</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Can't I say that what the Format Space rote does it's </span><i>similar</i><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> to create a temporary (and barren) Horizon Realm?. Because if I can now the Rote isn't an isolated piece of rules that can't be compared with anything else.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Do Horizon Realms null </span><i>every</i><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> other kind of power? . </span><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Well, usualy not, but maybe. There isn't much written on the matter. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">There's one thing. </span><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Autochtonia, in the very old Book of Chantries, was deemed to be the most Technocratic world of the Technocracy. Paradox here, for mystic mages, was </span><i>far worse</i><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> than in the normal world (in a botched spell, you die). It was said that even vampires suffered a smalish form of Paradox while in there, and it was said in a way that suggested this wasn't usual. </span><span style=\"font-size:13px\">From this I gather two things: 1 Alteration of &quot;fundamental r</span><span style=\"font-size:13px\">eality&quot; </span><i>could </i><span style=\"font-size:13px\">be able to affect other supernatural powers (keep in mind that the sources fot this kind of stuff are very obscure). 2 Mages are always more affected by this &quot;reality field&quot; than other powers.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">In general it's assumed that supernatural creatures are, at the bare minimum, </span><i>resistant</i><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> to this wibbiy wobbly reality alteration stuff. Usually Paradox and Consensus are empty words for them. Curse of Caine it's an actual Constant, that can't be changed, never, ever, nowhere, without incuring in the full wrath of Paradox, above and beyond normal rules, and Disciplines come directly from that source. So it's the Triat, and Gaia doesn't need to be below that.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">That being said, I think this it's the key issue with crossover: </span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">And pitting the forces of the wyrm against mages completely destroys the very story niche the wyrm is meant to inhabit. Entropy is not absolute in mage. The world isn't spiralling to some pre destined end. There is no future but the ones mankind makes for themselves.</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Because this it's true, you need to make a compromise. Otherwise it's not crossover, and the BSD are not Garou, they're just sturdy Bygones that dindn't get the memo that their world ended. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">If Garou and Vampires are that, then they should get the same treatment as dragons, unicorns, and all other beasts that had to jump on the &quot;Verbena train&quot; out of the world. Heck, vampires almost comply with that characterization by being &quot;thaumnivores&quot; already (with a clever, if unexplained, way of getting the juice). Our &quot;Consensus Friendly&quot; Lupines? should be </span><span style=\"font-size:13px\">thaumnivores too (which they aren't).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Because all the lines assume their monsters are super important and a power to be reckon with, and because WoD aothors tried to create a crossover world, Mage had to adopt lousy excuses like: &quot;oh well, but THESE supernaturals are special, you see, they're accepted into the Subconcious Consensus (but dragons didn't?)&quot;. </span><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The reason of these excuses it's to make them able to do all that they do without Paradox kicking their asses. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">And now, bcause you have,a new cool Rote, you think you can avoid that editiorial command?, Nah, it's easier to come with more excuses: &quot;Oh well, but THESE supers are ingrained into the Constants, their power cannot be supressed&quot;, or even a more studied: &quot;Oh well, the Rote generates conditions similar to that of a Horizon Realm, OK, Garou can use Gifts, but they're at +3 difficulty like if they were in a Realm hostile to their mojo&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">But my point is this: There are no rules that enforce what you said. There are </span><i>apparent </i><span style=\"font-size:13px\">rules, but they were not intended for Crossover and crossover breaks mage assumptions ALL the time. Crossover ALWAYS demands special rules...because the last part of your post it's totally true.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T15:52:42-07:00","id":1133974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133844#post1133844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Antimatter. Not nukes. Cleaner.</div> </div> </div> </div>It still gives off a gamma ray emission, which can still empower the furmlings inside the Umbral half of a massive Thunderwyrm's circulatory system or down in the guts of a particular Hive. Or possibly give rise to something worse, since shovels in Werewolf tend to end up digging deeper holes rather than being used to climb out of the hole that everyone is already in, and military hardware is an almost certainly guaranteed shovel launched down the shaft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T16:08:25-07:00","id":1133977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133974#post1133974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It still gives off a gamma ray emission, which can still empower the furmlings inside the Umbral half of a massive Thunderwyrm's circulatory system or down in the guts of a particular Hive. Or possibly give rise to something worse, since shovels in Werewolf tend to end up digging deeper holes rather than being used to climb out of the hole that everyone is already in, and military hardware is an almost certainly guaranteed shovel launched down the shaft.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence why you unmake everything in that chunk of Umbra as part of the assaults.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T16:25:38-07:00","id":1133982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133977#post1133977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hence why you unmake everything in that chunk of Umbra as part of the assaults.</div> </div> </div> </div>...You do know that one of the appellations of the Wyrm is the Unmaker, right? Doesn't it perhaps strike you as a bit hazardous to assume that you can unmake the Unmaker's brood? As in something could go horribly, terribly wrong and lead to some truly terribly shit for the Mages who try, like accidentally creating Paradox Banes or something along that line of awfulness?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T17:47:47-07:00","id":1134001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133982#post1133982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...You do know that one of the appellations of the Wyrm is the Unmaker, right? Doesn't it perhaps strike you as a bit hazardous to assume that you can unmake the Unmaker's brood? As in something could go horribly, terribly wrong and lead to some truly terribly shit for the Mages who try, like accidentally creating Paradox Banes or something along that line of awfulness?</div> </div> </div> </div>He sucks at it. I mean seriously. His only opposition is a few tribes of furry captain planets who can't stop killing EACH OTHER for absolutely idiotic reasons even when faced with litteral apocalyptic oblivion and he STILL HASN'T WON yet.<br /> <br /> The Wyrm is an overblown captain planet villain, nothing more. What is 'Apocalypse' to garou is little more than 'Tuesday' to Mage. And this is, again, why I don't advise mixing the two settings in more than a tangential manner. You make one or the other the 'prime' setting depending on what the majority of your players are playing and what the game is about.<br /> <br /> If Werewolf is the prime setting, the Wyrm is unstoppable and all powerful etc etc.<br /> <br /> If Mage is the Prime Setting, the Wyrm is potent but just as vulnerable to being vaporized as any other umbral being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T23:21:19-07:00","id":1134064,"title":"","content":"Without even getting into crossover dissonance, Wyrm-spirits can be destroyed. Being part of the &quot;unmaker's&quot; brood doesn't automatically grant you immortality, invulnerability, or cause you to can power when hit by damaging attacks but lose power when hit with buffs.<br /> <br /> In Mage, sure, there's always a chance things go wrong (though &quot;Paradox Banes&quot; aren't a thing in the game), but for a coordinated planned massive assault those chances are very small.<br /> <br /> That said that, mages can't tangle with the Wyrm itself (or even one of the triatic heads). Mages can get extremely potent with their anti-spirit stuff, but by Mage's on setting, the higher powers that be level spirits aren't something they can take on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T23:36:35-07:00","id":1134067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133838#post1133838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most perceived problems of crossover come because one assumes that *my* magical thing it's going to be super effective just because nothing says it won't. Ignoring that the material most likely wasn't written with every gameline and every situation in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. So, so, so much this. I would like this statement more than once if it were allowed. <br /> This sort of argument comes up way too often on these forums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T23:59:21-07:00","id":1134075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134001#post1134001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He sucks at it. I mean seriously. His only opposition is a few tribes of furry captain planets</div> </div> </div> </div>Full stop, Captain Planet is firmly in the style of Mage. One of the key ways you can tell is that no one in the show guts their antagonists in a fit of rage.<br /> <br /> (More seriously, they basically have a shared avatar that appears to them as some vision of &quot;Gaia&quot;. That's how it basically clicks in. From there, you add in standard Mage plots - time travel, bizarre gadgets that are basically magical plot fiat, and a suspicious lack of animism beyond one &quot;spirit of the earth&quot;.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> who can't stop killing EACH OTHER for absolutely idiotic reasons even when faced with litteral apocalyptic oblivion and he STILL HASN'T WON yet. </div> </div> </div>Because the Garou have actually managed to defeat them time and again when they had old fashioned approaches. The werewolves are good at what they do, and what they do is not nice, bordering on horrific.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Wyrm is an overblown captain planet villain, nothing more. What is 'Apocalypse' to garou is little more than 'Tuesday' to Mage. And this is, again, why I don't advise mixing the two settings in more than a tangential manner. You make one or the other the 'prime' setting depending on what the majority of your players are playing and what the game is about. </div> </div> </div>The Wyrm is Cthulhu, or the Dark Side of the Force. You don't fight it. You destroy manifestations of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Werewolf is the prime setting, the Wyrm is unstoppable and all powerful etc etc.<br /> <br /> If Mage is the Prime Setting, the Wyrm is potent but just as vulnerable to being vaporized as any other umbral being. </div> </div> </div>That's not how that works in either case. You don't vaporize a being bigger than a Celestine in either game. You can't even comprehend its true form, no matter how high your Spirit or Gnosis is; this isn't some Incarna that's big but still somewhat relatable. It's a third of the cosmos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 08-26-2017, 03:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T00:05:24-07:00","id":1134077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134064#post1134064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without even getting into crossover dissonance, Wyrm-spirits can be destroyed. Being part of the &quot;unmaker's&quot; brood doesn't automatically grant you immortality, invulnerability, or cause you to can power when hit by damaging attacks but lose power when hit with buffs.<br /> <br /> In Mage, sure, there's always a chance things go wrong (though &quot;Paradox Banes&quot; aren't a thing in the game)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that was the point. They aren't a thing, but if you go around assuming that you can perfectly sterilize every Hive you come across, you might just end up with your very own Storm Eater, except that instead of consuming Wyld-spirits, it eats Avatars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T09:28:25-07:00","id":1134156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134075#post1134075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not how that works in either case. You don't vaporize a being bigger than a Celestine in either game. You can't even comprehend its true form, no matter how high your Spirit or Gnosis is; this isn't some Incarna that's big but still somewhat relatable. It's a third of the cosmos.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how mage metaphysics works. That's how certain mages beliefs about mage metaphysics works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T09:29:16-07:00","id":1134157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133421#post1133421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? Where is this written/said?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the rules of what Mage magic can do? In past flavor fiction?<br /> <br /> Obviously, this Hive is not threat level RAGNAROK, but I'm sure they have a cool name for the kind of threat such a Pit represents. It may not warrant spirit nukes or orbital mirrors, but there IS going to be a protocol. The Union is the direct heir of the Order of Reason with significant institutional memory. They have files. They have mages whose job it is to be able to access those files. Progenitors dissect Werewolves. Protecting humanity from things like BSDs is part of the Union's mission statement. Maybe even Job 1/Prime Directive. If not, it's 2nd or 3rd. Any ideas that the the Union is &quot;blind&quot; to such threats because their Uber-Focus doesn't allow for it are pretty much drek. The Union has its explanation for the broad strokes of the entirety of the supernatural aspects of the WoD. They have people whose job is to do EXACTLY these things. (And BSD antics aren't even remotely &quot;invisible&quot; to anyone with Dim Sci 1. Out of sight, out of mind, sure. But with Correspondence 2, if the Technocrats are looking in the right place... And if this is the sort of situation that could develop into a serious problem, it might just have tweaked some analyst out there who is using Correspondence/Entropy/Time effects to develop their threat projections.)<br /> <br /> So, vide what Heavy Arms said. Maybe fuel-air bombs or low-yield tactical nukes (with &quot;rapid dissipation radiation&quot;). Maybe not from orbit, but good luck for the BSD's seeing the stealthed bombers (and bombs) in the troposphere, shooting missiles on highly angled trajectories. And that's all pretty much Coincidental. As for all the Sleeper witnesses? It depends on where the Hive is as to what protocol is going to be in play (from &quot;evacuation due to hazardous materials&quot; to &quot;acceptable casualties&quot;, and that might even mean &quot;kill all the Sleepers with something coincidental so we can be as Vulgar as we need to be&quot;) with the emphasis on getting Sleeper Witnesses out of the way in case things are dire enough to get the authorization to go full-on Vulgar and do things like aport the explosive devices directly into the Hive. Repeated until the area is a smoking crater. (A meteorite impact?)<br /> <br /> Assuming, of course, the Union is the Union described. Which seems like a reasonable basic assumption, since this question is on the Mage board, not the Werewolf or general boards.<br /> <br /> Maybe, if the Union is Nephandi-riddled as per the default timeline, there might be a difference, but probably not. That's a great diversion from looking for rot from within. <br /> <br /> Possibly, if mages are fairly thin on the ground, it might go down differently. The thinner the more likely it might slip through the cracks. Though this level of shitstorm seems like it would eventually come to their attention. The later, the more drastic the level of response would probably need to be. If the Garou do their jobs and deal with the problem, the Union might just have to bat clean-up and send in MiBs to explain away what happened. In fact, the Union might just use the minimal level of effort needed and that would probably be to allow and enable those who are fanatical experts in these matters to deal with the core problem and then just bat clean-up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T10:04:27-07:00","id":1134166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134077#post1134077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that was the point. They aren't a thing, but if you go around assuming that you can perfectly sterilize every Hive you come across, you might just end up with your very own Storm Eater, except that instead of consuming Wyld-spirits, it eats Avatars.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you don't, because they aren't a thing in the game, you can't create them by accident because that's not something the game has happen. That's not how any of this works.<br /> <br /> This response is also verging far too much into &quot;ST fiat&quot; level responses. The Union can't worry about stuff an ST might make up just to add consequences to their actions beyond the basic rules, because that would require them to be able to recognize they're fictional characters inside an RPG. Not that sterilizing a hive comes close to something like the release of Storm Eater, or the events that unleashed the Avatar Storm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134157#post1134157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe, if the Union is Nephandi-riddled as per the default timeline, there might be a difference, but probably not. That's a great diversion from looking for rot from within.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even with the worst version of the Nephandi take over of the Union, things don't change much for this. The Nephandi love to use other corrupted entities as pawns to distract other mages from what they're up to. Strikes against hives and pits might be worse in this circumstance, as the Nephandi that took over the Technocracy use them as convenient targets to keep the uncorrupted members busy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T23:15:08-07:00","id":1134365,"title":"","content":"My view of the subject is I'm entirely comfortable with the WORLD of Darkness and all the gamelines but to do that, I have to accept no group is fundamentally more awesome than anyone else.<br /> <br /> It's like STREETFIGHTER: THE RPG.<br /> <br /> Remember that?<br /> <br /> Everyone can beat everyone else under the right circumstances because the games break down if Ryu is the bestest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T23:43:31-07:00","id":1134369,"title":"","content":"Allow me to write a bit of fiction as a five year author and gamer of 25+ years.<br /> <br /> Memo 1#:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">TO: ADRIAN NEWBERRY, CEO OF PENTEX<br /> FROM: MARCUS WHITAKER, PENTEX FIRST TEAM 38#<br /> RE: THE JAW TOOTH HIVE INCIDENT<br /> <br /> Well, this is a complete cluster[expletive redacted], I tell you. I'm standing here, right now in 200 foot deep sink hole which is surrounded by a bunch of other sink holes. Some serious [expletive deleted] went down here and I'm not sure how to begin to explain it. Anna, she's our psychic, tried to read just went down and she ended up swallowing her own tongue. Not that such is uncommon but it's going to take awhile to regenerate. The best thing I can describe is the Jaw Tooth Hive is gone along with all of its members and we're going to need to find out why. I don't think the Puppies did this or we'd be in a hell of a lot more trouble than usual. It looks like Tunguska out here.</span><br /> <br /> Memo 2#:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">TO: MARCUS WHITAKER, PENTEX FIRST TEAM 38#<br /> FROM: ADRIAN NEWBERRY, CEO OF PENTEX<br /> RE: RE: THE JAW TOOTH HIVE INCIDENT</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Leave this matter alone.</span><br /> <br /> Memo 3#:<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">TO: MARCUS WHITAKER, PENTEX FIRST TEAM 38#<br /> FROM: ADRIAN NEWBERRY, CEO OF PENTEX<br /> RE: RE: RE: THE JAW TOOTH HIVE INCIDENT</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">I am frustrated to say I have been informed by our primary shareholder that you are to be brought into the loop regarding this incident. Apparently, the Breach Project were were going to use the Jaw Tooth Hive for is important enough that we need to find some substitutes and we can't have the individuals involved in this incident tripping over it. That is why you are going to read in on this information and you alone. Remember, we DO know who you tell these things. As you may guess, we on the board know more about what happened to the Jaw Tooth Hive than you do, and we know who is responsible.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">In this case, it is a secret society called the Technocratic Union which, essentially, functions as a roughly equal-sized entity to Pentex and dabbles in many of the same businesses we do (bio-genetics, cybernetics, psychic abilities, and the extermination of troublesome supernatural entities). It is, despite this, incredibly stupid and in abject denial about other dimensions as well as beings like our Friends Upstairs. Despite its vast wealth and surprising military might, possessing a private army larger than any other on Earth (even our own), they are generally unwitting servants of the Weaver. Recently, we had to bring home a department we had infiltrated of their group and have been keeping one of its branches [see enclosed &quot;Syndicate&quot; file] pacified with large checks they are only too happy to take.<br /> <br /> In general, the Union does not bother us or our allies. They are too interested in a ideological war against a group of mystical religious fundamentalists which occupies the majority of their time and resources. They have a &quot;target of opportunity&quot; policy with many supernaturals but the simple fact is they need the vampires to do the grunt work of covering up the supernatural's existence and misunderstand the place of the Wolves in the universe due to their, again, appalling ignorance. In this case, their discovery of the Jaw Tooth Hive seems to be due to one of their agents mistaking it as a &quot;Nephandus Labyrinth&quot; which functions essentially as a Hive for magic-users.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">The Union dispatched a group of &quot;Men in Black&quot; to investigate, expecting minimum resistance but were immediately alerted by the Hive's banes and were promptly slaughtered by the Black Spiral Dancers within. If not for this action, they may have been content to simply monitor the Hive due to the aforementioned stretched resources. Instead, it became an issue of pride for the local Comptroller who promptly dispatched their local facilities resources to exterminate the Hive's population. Given this was a important facility with over 30 Wolves and several packs of Formori, it was a slaughter.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">The Technocracy does not like to lose and what followed was an increasing use of larger, more nasty devices designed to reduce the target to ashes, including assistance from a group of theirs which actually is aware of other-dimensions called the Void Engineers. What was dispatched were devices designed to &quot;sanitize&quot; the Node plus large numbers of artificial beings essentially used as cannon fodder. With the assistance of weapons designed to kill spirits as well as devices capable of detecting them, they laid a number of explosives in the tunnels and collapsed them before burning the Spirit world for approximately 5 acres in five places. Casualties for the Union are difficult to estimate but I'd wager 6-1 in the Hive's favor with the majority of casualties being brainwashed soldiers and biological constructs.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">You might call this a &quot;victory&quot; for the Union but, like their war with the Traditions, it has effectively crippled their operations in the area for the next few decades. My personal suggestion is we increase our presence there as well as work to &quot;meditate&quot; between the Black Spiral Dancers Hives wanting vengeance and direct them back to their traditional foes. The Union doesn't need more victories like this so let them congratulate themselves while we reap the benefits. They don't need to know there's hundreds of Hives like Jaw Tooth.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-27-2017, 02:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T09:44:21-07:00","id":1134504,"title":"","content":"Except it wouldn't even take an Adept, much less a Master to wreck untold havoc from a secure lab a hundred miles away. Correspondence 2/Forces 2/Prime 2. Quantum tunneling causing localized fluctuations in space-time manifesting as atomic level variances creating thermal overload. Pinpoint the strikes with satellite imagery. Werewolves still take Agg from Fire. Just keep pouring it in. Maybe three to five teams with another on oversight?<br /> <br /> Vulgar as Hell, but I'm sure the Operatives will be able to explain the necessity in the required paperwork. They will probably have copies of appropriate authorizations to attach. Even a fun-sized level of the Technocracy is an organization founded in cooperative effort. If they are aware of the problem before the sandwyrms ridden by spell-slinging mutant werewolves aren't already rampaging across the countryside, they should be able to deal with problem in such a way as Pentex would be going from &quot;Something is getting out of hand&quot; to &quot;Oh shit! What the Hell just happened?&quot; While the disinformation starts showing up in &quot;Breaking News&quot;. The issue is more, &quot;Does the Technocracy become aware and at what point and is the situation given the priority handling it warrants?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T12:34:21-07:00","id":1134565,"title":"","content":"Well, most werewolves take Agg from fire, some are going to have Master of Fire and all that. Still going to do a lot of damage despite that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T12:50:48-07:00","id":1134579,"title":"","content":"Maybe not terribly helpful, but it is worth noting (from my point of view) that the example given was a level 5 Hive, of which there <i>might be</i> just 1 or 2 on the planet. This isn't just any Hive we are talking about. This should be one of the strongest Wyrm fortresses in the Material world. And if you are assuming an integrated WoD, then it must have defenses that have allowed it to exist for so long in the face of Garou, Mages (of all stripes) and many other forces/enemies. This isn't (in any way) to say that it can't be taken down. Just that the measures required to do so should be at or just below the project Ragnarok.<br /> <br /> Now obviously, lower level Hives require far less resources to combat. But I think the root of the issue is one that is always at the core of discussions like this. If the WoD were fully integrated, then it wouldn't work at all like any of the individual game line's portray. Mage does to accept that there are possibly hundreds of thousands of fomori running around the mundane world. Werewolf similarly does not accept that there are so many Mages (anywhere from 7,000 to 45000 depending on which book you want to cite). The Setting just doesn't work with so many supernaturals present. And this is to say nothing of the other Supernatural populations (Vampires, Wraiths, Changelings, etc.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T13:49:18-07:00","id":1134597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134565#post1134565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, most werewolves take Agg from fire, some are going to have Master of Fire and all that. Still going to do a lot of damage despite that.</div> </div> </div> </div>And soak Gifts, which are arguably more important since they can completely eliminate fire damage altogether. Between that and Crinos having a minimum of 4 dice to soak fire damage, the mages might just run out of resources before the Hive does. If the bane totem of the pit helps out or they use a rite to capitalize on a pit's strengths, the mages will probably buckle before the Dancers do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T14:54:37-07:00","id":1134625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134597#post1134597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And soak Gifts, which are arguably more important since they can completely eliminate fire damage altogether. Between that and Crinos having a minimum of 4 dice to soak fire damage, the mages might just run out of resources before the Hive does. If the bane totem of the pit helps out or they use a rite to capitalize on a pit's strengths, the mages will probably buckle before the Dancers do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the counterarguments to this are going to be:<br /> 1) System-wise, Mage encourages abuse and so the Mages can just build up as many successes as they need to overcome whatever amount of soak a target will have (if it isn't outright immune). In crossovers, Mage is basically unbeatable because of how the dice rolling is set up for Rituals. This has almost nothing to do with how the Setting is set up though which is typically overlooked in these discussions (in my experience).<br /> <br /> 2) The damage doesn't have to be fire. Fire is one of those things that comes a lot so there are plenty of defenses against it (I can think of several Gifts off the top of my head). But since Forces doesn't care about energy source really, the damage could just as easily come from sound, cold, electricity, etc. And when talking about this sort of conflict, the Mage players typically argue (again, in my experience) that any and all Spheres you need are available at whatever levels and so the damage will probably always be some sort of unique anti-spirit radiation mcguffin that can't be defended against, regardless.<br /> <br /> 3) Using Correspondence/Dimensional Science/whatever else, the Technocracy can just kill whatever enemies it wants by firing Far Umbral weapons arrays with a near infinite (effectively) amount of successes anywhere on Earth (or otherwise) for an automatic &quot;I win&quot; button. Again, it makes zero sense in Setting but that doesn't seem to have ever mattered.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T14:56:51-07:00","id":1134627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134504#post1134504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except it wouldn't even take an Adept, much less a Master to wreck untold havoc from a secure lab a hundred miles away. Correspondence 2/Forces 2/Prime 2. Quantum tunneling causing localized fluctuations in space-time manifesting as atomic level variances creating thermal overload. Pinpoint the strikes with satellite imagery. Werewolves still take Agg from Fire. Just keep pouring it in. Maybe three to five teams with another on oversight?<br /> <br /> Vulgar as Hell, but I'm sure the Operatives will be able to explain the necessity in the required paperwork. They will probably have copies of appropriate authorizations to attach. Even a fun-sized level of the Technocracy is an organization founded in cooperative effort. If they are aware of the problem before the sandwyrms ridden by spell-slinging mutant werewolves aren't already rampaging across the countryside, they should be able to deal with problem in such a way as Pentex would be going from &quot;Something is getting out of hand&quot; to &quot;Oh shit! What the Hell just happened?&quot; While the disinformation starts showing up in &quot;Breaking News&quot;. The issue is more, &quot;Does the Technocracy become aware and at what point and is the situation given the priority handling it warrants?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you, if the Technocracy could do that, they wouldn't need the Men in Black or HIT Marks.<br /> <br /> Remember, the Technocracy never can do Vulgar Magic.<br /> <br /> They always need foci and a Correspondence 2/Forces 2/Prime 2 rote is a Drone strike.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T15:52:18-07:00","id":1134643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134579#post1134579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe not terribly helpful, but it is worth noting (from my point of view) that the example given was a level 5 Hive, of which there <i>might be</i> just 1 or 2 on the planet. This isn't just any Hive we are talking about. This should be one of the strongest Wyrm fortresses in the Material world. And if you are assuming an integrated WoD, then it must have defenses that have allowed it to exist for so long in the face of Garou, Mages (of all stripes) and many other forces/enemies. This isn't (in any way) to say that it can't be taken down. Just that the measures required to do so should be at or just below the project Ragnarok.<br /> <br /> Now obviously, lower level Hives require far less resources to combat. But I think the root of the issue is one that is always at the core of discussions like this. If the WoD were fully integrated, then it wouldn't work at all like any of the individual game line's portray. Mage does to accept that there are possibly hundreds of thousands of fomori running around the mundane world. Werewolf similarly does not accept that there are so many Mages (anywhere from 7,000 to 45000 depending on which book you want to cite). The Setting just doesn't work with so many supernaturals present. And this is to say nothing of the other Supernatural populations (Vampires, Wraiths, Changelings, etc.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Why then, does North Korea exist? There are any number of reasons for why an entity can exist beyond &quot;Being tough enough that noone can take down.&quot; There is &quot;Being tough enough to take down that it's not a sufficient return on investment.&quot; for example, Much like North Korea. If there's no GAIN that equals the costs then the only ones who will attack are those who are blinded by ideology.<br /> <br /> But we're talking about the Technocracy. The people who can have level <b><i>20</i></b> nodes. These are the people with enough raw power and enlightened resources, and an infrastructure in place for getting those resources to the places they are needed to call down a litteral beam of purifying light from on high <i>and outright ignore the paradox costs.</i><br /> <br /> And given among their skill sets mind control is not the least of them, the hive is lucky if they <i>only</i> end up killed. The other alternative is that they implement mind procedures from afar, (via propaganda) and suddenly the Hive is in civil war with itself between those corrupted by the technocrats propaganda and those who aren't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134627#post1134627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mind you, if the Technocracy could do that, they wouldn't need the Men in Black or HIT Marks.<br /> <br /> Remember, the Technocracy never can do Vulgar Magic.<br /> <br /> They always need foci and a Correspondence 2/Forces 2/Prime 2 rote is a Drone strike.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>~ _<br /> 0_0<br /> <br /> Technocrats most certainly CAN use Vulgar magic. HIT Marks are an example of it.<br /> <br /> And 'requiring foci' does not mean 'requires a foci that makes sense to modern technology'<br /> <br /> Having some sort of resonance array to cause ripples in space-time that create the desired effect, and the 'ritual' is a number of enlightened scientists running around it twiddling knobs and pushing buttons to alter settings on the device to keep it on the desired course is just as much within the technocracies purview as a drone strike.<br /> <br /> Honestly, a drone strike isn't even magic. It's just mundane tech at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11744,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","user":"Enginseer-42","date":". 08-27-2017, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T17:21:51-07:00","id":1134668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134597#post1134597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And soak Gifts, which are arguably more important since they can completely eliminate fire damage altogether. Between that and Crinos having a minimum of 4 dice to soak fire damage, the mages might just run out of resources before the Hive does. If the bane totem of the pit helps out or they use a rite to capitalize on a pit's strengths, the mages will probably buckle before the Dancers do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Soak Gifts aren't that much to rely on. The only one that's going to be common in a Hive is already a Rank 2 BSD Gift, and is +3 soak dice. The other Rank 2 Soak Gifts are in the Gaian Tribal lists, and are roll dependent. Above that (and more rare for it) most of the Soak boosts are generally big boosts, but highly situational ones (like massive Soak boosts against specific elements, or massive general Soak boosts, but sacrificing most other actions, all those Metis BSDs with Shell aren't exactly helping the hypothetical fight much).<br /> <br /> The problem with mages &quot;running out of resources,&quot; is that Mage doesn't really work that way. Garou that burn through their Rage, Gnosis, and WP quickly find themselves at fairly reduced combat ability as they lose access to all sorts of Gifts and the like once they run out of points to activate things with. Mages almost never need to spend points. Mages throw WP and Quintessence at effects so they're stronger, rather than as requirements (save for the rare spell that requires Quint). Quintessence in particular is less of a problem for most mages, because they can store large amounts of it (20 personally, plus huge amounts in quint battery Wonders if they want them or are provided them for a mission), and spells can be spent to gather more.<br /> <br /> Battles of attrition are not in a Garou's favor against the Technocracy specifically. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134625#post1134625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">System-wise, Mage encourages abuse and so the Mages can just build up as many successes as they need to overcome whatever amount of soak a target will have (if it isn't outright immune).</div> </div> </div> </div>System-wise, Mage encourages creativity, not abuse.<br /> <br /> And there are limits to how many successes a mage can gather, the problem for non-mages is that their damage output is extremely high per success. Mage is calibrated around what a lone mage is going to do on a single roll (which is why the common wisdom for fighting mages is to attack them when they're caught off guard). What a team of mages can do with preparation is nuts. It's not even any sort of 'abuse' it's just the RAW.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In crossovers, Mage is basically unbeatable because of how the dice rolling is set up for Rituals. This has almost nothing to do with how the Setting is set up though which is typically overlooked in these discussions (in my experience). </div> </div> </div>Actually, it's perfectly in-line with how the setting is set up. Mages are supposed to value rituals because it's how they get big effects done, but it means having to spend time on rituals which is an opportunity cost. Mages with time can magic their way through a lot of issues, while mages running on the fly are significantly weaker. That's how the setting says things are supposed to be. The only places this tends to not match up with the setting as written are when the Tremere need to not be eliminated by the Hermetics (which is why there was the rule that Thamaturgic Counter Magic could defend against Hermetics, and later M20's more general ability for nightfolk to countermagic).<br /> <br /> But, you know, it's just Mage fans not arguing in good faith. Sure that's going to go over well in the Mage forum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And when talking about this sort of conflict, the Mage players typically argue (again, in my experience) that any and all Spheres you need are available at whatever levels and so the damage will probably always be some sort of unique anti-spirit radiation mcguffin that can't be defended against, regardless. </div> </div> </div>Or, you know, we're talking about the Technocracy that manufactures anti-spirit grenades for their operatives to use, and can arm their forces with as much silver weaponry as they want. And the Union is operating to maximize the spread of Spheres effectively among their forces. Most individual operatives don't need all the Spheres, they need spreads that are frequently within starting level values, as different specialists handle different problems. As well, a lot of the higher level stuff can be done in preparation so that's less of a concern with the Union's infrastructure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) Using Correspondence/Dimensional Science/whatever else, the Technocracy can just kill whatever enemies it wants by firing Far Umbral weapons arrays with a near infinite (effectively) amount of successes anywhere on Earth (or otherwise) for an automatic &quot;I win&quot; button. Again, it makes zero sense in Setting but that doesn't seem to have ever mattered. </div> </div> </div>According to the setting, as has been mentioned, the Technocracy has an orbital sun beam weapon designed for eliminating powerful vampires. So yeah, this sort of thing is actually in line with the setting.<br /> <br /> For all the complaints about how that &quot;doesn't seem to have ever mattered&quot; to Mage fans, you don't seem to be particularly worried about actually presenting the setting accurately.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T18:00:51-07:00","id":1134683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134668#post1134668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Soak Gifts aren't that much to rely on. The only one that's going to be common in a Hive is already a Rank 2 BSD Gift, and is +3 soak dice. The other Rank 2 Soak Gifts are in the Gaian Tribal lists, and are roll dependent. Above that (and more rare for it) most of the Soak boosts are generally big boosts, but highly situational ones (like massive Soak boosts against specific elements, or massive general Soak boosts, but sacrificing most other actions, all those Metis BSDs with Shell aren't exactly helping the hypothetical fight much).<br /> <br /> The problem with mages &quot;running out of resources,&quot; is that Mage doesn't really work that way. Garou that burn through their Rage, Gnosis, and WP quickly find themselves at fairly reduced combat ability as they lose access to all sorts of Gifts and the like once they run out of points to activate things with. Mages almost never need to spend points. Mages throw WP and Quintessence at effects so they're stronger, rather than as requirements (save for the rare spell that requires Quint). Quintessence in particular is less of a problem for most mages, because they can store large amounts of it (20 personally, plus huge amounts in quint battery Wonders if they want them or are provided them for a mission), and spells can be spent to gather more.<br /> <br /> Battles of attrition are not in a Garou's favor against the Technocracy specifically.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm apparently still somewhat sleep deprived and forgot to delete &quot;running out of resources&quot;. I was talking about the proposed vulgarity of the effect and continued use of it building up Paradox vs. protective effects of tapping the pit or engaging in another form of caern rite to make the effect more trouble than it's worth. Bane Totem effects could also come into play, especially if something is furmling-friendly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> System-wise, Mage encourages creativity, not abuse. </div> </div> </div>Is there a system that doesn't encourage abuse of some sort? Eventually, the break points are going to reveal themselves, and people are going to flock to them. And seeing as how Mage hasn't changed much beyond the first edition player's guide and is kind of fast and loose with its open system, we're still dealing with a vast universe of exploitable loopholes that rely on STs shutting things down if they become a problem for an individual game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T20:43:52-07:00","id":1134732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134643#post1134643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But we're talking about the Technocracy. The people who can have level <b><i>20</i></b> nodes.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I could find, the background goes to 10 which M20 says is the equivalent of a level 5 Caern (which is the same thing as a Hive).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134643#post1134643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> These are the people with enough raw power and enlightened resources, and an infrastructure in place for getting those resources to the places they are needed to call down a litteral beam of purifying light from on high <i>and outright ignore the paradox costs.</i><br /> <br /> And given among their skill sets mind control is not the least of them, the hive is lucky if they <i>only</i> end up killed. The other alternative is that they implement mind procedures from afar, (via propaganda) and suddenly the Hive is in civil war with itself between those corrupted by the technocrats propaganda and those who aren't.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the exact sort of argument I was referring to. And I actually believe it is possible system-wise. Which makes the existence of non Mage Antagonists kind of silly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134668#post1134668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For all the complaints about how that &quot;doesn't seem to have ever mattered&quot; to Mage fans, you don't seem to be particularly worried about actually presenting the setting accurately.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not actually complaining. If everything works as stated <u>System-wise</u> then Mage's only enemies would ever be Mages. The Technocracy can and should be able to eliminate every (non-Mage) Antagonist they have with a semi-complicated Ritual that does it all in one go, with no way for said faction to defend. That was entirely my point. System-wise, it's entirely possible. Unless I've misunderstood your statements, they support that position. The Setting however obviously does not. Mind you, I am just speaking from my experience seeing these arguments come up over and over again on here. The counter to any non-Mage faction is always that the Technocracy initiates some high cost (though cost is never actually discussed other than saying it's high) operation that destroys their enemy, regardless of power level or defenses. For examples, see the posts on the last few pages about how to destroy a level 5 hive.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T20:56:37-07:00","id":1134734,"title":"","content":"That actually really does jive with the fluff. Non-Mage Supernaturals are near universally dismissed as a non-threat in technocratic fluff. They're at best an annoyance, something that might impair operations at a crucial moment during the ACTUAL war with other mages. But the implication always is, and as far as I can tell, always was that the other supernaturals are the mystical equivalent to terrorists. Whereas the Traditions are the Soviet Union facing off with the Unions America. The other supernaturals can cause trouble. Do some damage. but really don't operate on the same scale at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T23:48:01-07:00","id":1134765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134683#post1134683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was talking about the proposed vulgarity of the effect and continued use of it building up Paradox vs. protective effects of tapping the pit or engaging in another form of caern rite to make the effect more trouble than it's worth. Bane Totem effects could also come into play, especially if something is furmling-friendly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradox doesn't exactly build up that fast. Even if you're using the Revised rules, the Technocrats can spend a WP to deal with the Paradox after the fight is over instead of during it should it become a problem. That even assumes things like carpet bombing a Hive's physical side get vulgar just because they're adding some oomph to it. Bombs that also increase the Gauntlet and shred any manifested spirits aren't exactly prone to vulgarity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there a system that doesn't encourage abuse of some sort? </div> </div> </div>Encourage and allow are different things. Every system having break points doesn't mean the game is encouraging you to seek them out and exploit them.<br /> <br /> Mage putting a lot of the break points in the social contract of RPGs doesn't mean it encourages abuse, it just means that's where the break points tend to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134732#post1134732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the exact sort of argument I was referring to. And I actually believe it is possible system-wise. Which makes the existence of non Mage Antagonists kind of silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except this logic doesn't work. You're basically saying that because the US has nukes, citizens of the US should never be worried about being stabbed.<br /> <br /> Non-mage antagonists in Mage work just fine, because mages don't whip out things like the orbital anti-vampire satellite over a Sabbat shovel head causing some problems, just like the US doesn't drop a nuke in response to an American tourist getting robbed in some other country.<br /> <br /> The thing about this particular thread is that we're talking about something on the scale of the US vs. Somalia. If the US wanted to level Somalia, we could, easily. If we don't think that's the right approach, but want to take military action... we risk things like what happened in the Battle of Mogadishu where the US military got its ass handed to it. Making non-mage antagonists relevant in Mage is about keeping things out of the scale where a significant amount of the Union's offensive magical might is going to be called on.<br /> <br /> It takes a lot to get the Union to put everything aside to unleash the kind of force needed to just wipe out a Hive. That's why I tried to put the focus in my first post on &quot;if the Technocracy realizes the threat,&quot; as such an important consideration. There's reasons why the US doesn't unleash it's full military force, even when it could viably &quot;win&quot; a situation. <br /> <br /> As well, even in mage-on-mage conflicts, the majority of people involved aren't actually mages. Mages are rare, and don't have an easy way to create new mages. That means most mages are extremely conservative about putting mage lives at risk, when they can outfit allies to fight on the front lines, and influence from a distance (which does in fact limit their effectiveness in terms of what you can do with each spell). For every mage in the Union, there's hundreds of indoctrinated proles that can operate hypertech without incurring paradox. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If everything works as stated <u>System-wise</u> then Mage's only enemies would ever be Mages. The Technocracy can and should be able to eliminate every (non-Mage) Antagonist they have with a semi-complicated Ritual that does it all in one go, with no way for said faction to defend. </div> </div> </div>The system doesn't allow this. There are limits to what even the most powerful mages can do with one ritual, no matter how many helpers they have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The counter to any non-Mage faction is always that the Technocracy initiates some high cost (though cost is never actually discussed other than saying it's high) operation that destroys their enemy, regardless of power level or defenses. For examples, see the posts on the last few pages about how to destroy a level 5 hive. </div> </div> </div>Because that's the Technocracy's greatest strength. They are the best faction in the WoD at organizing and applying massive amounts of force.<br /> <br /> We're not talking about all of the Wyrm's servants and the entire Technocracy getting into one massive battle. We're talking about a single Hive getting smashed by the entire Technocracy's heavy hitting fast response military operations.<br /> <br /> And the cost isn't discussed, because the Union works like a government. They're capable of delaying the impact of the costs until an operation is over (at least until it's been going on for years). It costs them a lot to pull off an operation like this, but it's largely stuff they stock pile, and can refill those stock piles if they dip into them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T12:12:42-07:00","id":1134892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We're not talking about all of the Wyrm's servants and the entire Technocracy getting into one massive battle. We're talking about a single Hive getting smashed by the entire Technocracy's heavy hitting fast response military operations. </div> </div> </div>Aren't we, though? For what I take in this thread, that single Hive seems to be the neuralgic center of Wyrm operations in Earth, revered by all BSD. It probably can count with the Masters of Malfean Nephandi as &quot;minions&quot;, while counting with help of the entirety of Pentex.<br /> <br /> Perhaps your Somalia it's the Moskov of idpersona.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-28-2017, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T12:55:45-07:00","id":1134906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134892#post1134892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aren't we, though? For what I take in this thread, that single Hive seems to be the neuralgic center of Wyrm operations in Earth, revered by all BSD. It probably can count with the Masters of Malfean Nephandi as &quot;minions&quot;, while counting with help of the entirety of Pentex.<br /> <br /> Perhaps your Somalia it's the Moskov of idpersona.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose this is sort of my point. There are a handful of level 5 Hives in the entire world (I wouldn't say more than 3). And this discussion would have me to believe that they exist purely because the Technocracy doesn't see them as worth their time. But if for some reason they did, that these places would (relatively) easily be cleansed.<br /> <br /> And saying that the cost is high, but that it comes out of stockpiles that can be refilled at some later date. And that said resources have no definite amount. This to me makes the &quot;high&quot; cost meaningless. There is no reason the Technocracy shouldn't have eradicated (or claimed and cleansed) all non-Mage strongholds if this we're the case.<br /> And in my mind, the comparison of other Supernaturals to North Korea breaks down quickly. There are other superpowers that have a vested interest in NK that are comparable to the US. This isn't the case with this comparison. You don't have the Council of 9 aligned with the Garou or Vampires to protect them from the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Eh. Just how I see this. And the thread so far has mostly supported this view imo. And that sort of logic, in my mind, goes against the Setting as written. Specifically when you take into account the other game line's and not just looking at it from an exclusively Mage pov.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134765#post1134765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Except this logic doesn't work. You're basically saying that because the US has nukes, citizens of the US should never be worried about being stabbed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having free running Supernaturals makes sense in Setting (the equivalent of being stabbed to me). Other Supernaturals having extremely valuable resources the Technocracy would want (Caerns/Hives) does not. Not if they have the power to take said resources with little trouble or fear of effective retribution.<br /> <br /> Edit: Had more free time and figured I'd respond to some specific points:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134765#post1134765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The thing about this particular thread is that we're talking about something on the scale of the US vs. Somalia. If the US wanted to level Somalia, we could, easily. If we don't think that's the right approach, but want to take military action... we risk things like what happened in the Battle of Mogadishu where the US military got its ass handed to it. Making non-mage antagonists relevant in Mage is about keeping things out of the scale where a significant amount of the Union's offensive magical might is going to be called on. <br /> <br /> It takes a lot to get the Union to put everything aside to unleash the kind of force needed to just wipe out a Hive. That's why I tried to put the focus in my first post on &quot;if the Technocracy realizes the threat,&quot; as such an important consideration. There's reasons why the US doesn't unleash it's full military force, even when it could viably &quot;win&quot; a situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see the point you are making here, but I don't agree with the comparison. World politics is a different beast. There are other world powers that mitigate/effect plans of action like this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134765#post1134765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Because that's the Technocracy's greatest strength. They are the best faction in the WoD at organizing and applying massive amounts of force.</div> </div> </div> </div>So their greatest strength is the ability to win any conflict that can be solved by killing your opponent? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134765#post1134765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> We're not talking about all of the Wyrm's servants and the entire Technocracy getting into one massive battle. We're talking about a single Hive getting smashed by the entire Technocracy's heavy hitting fast response military operations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that we're talking about one of the most powerful of the Wyrm's strongholds (if we are still using the level 5 Hive as the focal point of this discussion) outside of the Realm of Malfeas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 08-28-2017, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T13:12:46-07:00","id":1134910,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of variations on the subject here because EVERY WORLD OF DARKNESS IS DIFFERENT.<br /> <br /> For example, Hive 5s are big huge and important things but not something like, &quot;This is the center of BSD activity in the world&quot;<br /> <br /> Not even close.<br /> <br /> But that's just my games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T13:24:18-07:00","id":1134918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134910#post1134910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a lot of variations on the subject here because EVERY WORLD OF DARKNESS IS DIFFERENT.<br /> <br /> For example, Hive 5s are big huge and important things but not something like, &quot;This is the center of BSD activity in the world&quot;<br /> <br /> Not even close.<br /> <br /> But that's just my games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, though even if a particular level 5 Hive isn't the center of the Spirals (arguments can certainly be made against that) it would still be a Wyrm fortress with hundreds (or more) of defenders and untold numbers of powers to call on. From my point of view, it has to be stressed that the example was a level 5 Hive. Not some random Hive somewhere in the world. The Hive/Caern Spirit alone, minus the army of defenders is going to be a being of immense power. And writing that off as &quot;Spirit solves this&quot; is a disservice to the Setting, even within just the Mage Setting 9without looking at the other main Splat books) I would say.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T13:36:55-07:00","id":1134924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134918#post1134918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough, though even if a particular level 5 Hive isn't the center of the Spirals (arguments can certainly be made against that) it would still be a Wyrm fortress with hundreds (or more) of defenders and untold numbers of powers to call on. From my point of view, it has to be stressed that the example was a level 5 Hive. Not some random Hive somewhere in the world. The Hive/Caern Spirit alone, minus the army of defenders is going to be a being of immense power. And writing that off as &quot;Spirit solves this&quot; is a disservice to the Setting, even within just the Mage Setting 9without looking at the other main Splat books) I would say.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's also how variations on caerns are handled. A Black Spiral Dancer Hive isn't necessarily going to be a fortress because it's a place of religious observance. Black Spiral Dancers gather there for rites and ceremonies plus there's probably hundreds of Banes around it but there's probably going to be only a few people there full time.<br /> <br /> The Central Park Sept isn't a fortress, it's a grassy knoll and it's level 3.<br /> <br /> Yes, there's people to guard it but most BSD packs are going to be out and about doing evil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T14:33:21-07:00","id":1134953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134924#post1134924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's also how variations on caerns are handled. A Black Spiral Dancer Hive isn't necessarily going to be a fortress because it's a place of religious observance. Black Spiral Dancers gather there for rites and ceremonies plus there's probably hundreds of Banes around it but there's probably going to be only a few people there full time.<br /> <br /> The Central Park Sept isn't a fortress, it's a grassy knoll and it's level 3.<br /> <br /> Yes, there's people to guard it but most BSD packs are going to be out and about doing evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well we certainly have different views on what a Caern is.<br /> It is not a church equivalent. As in a place you go now and then for religious observance. Certainly not the higher level ones.<br /> <br /> A level 5 Hive is likely to have several packs (of various Ranks) rotating caern protection along with the Elder Council and hundreds of banes (varying in power level from annoyance to powerhouse). Plus the demi-god powered Caern Spirit and additional mystical defenses.<br /> This is in addition to whatever other defenses it's going to have from various Wyrm Fera, probably a Nephandi or 2 and other weirdness (Thunderwyrms, visiting Incarna, portals to other Realms, etc). And this is also in addition to the possible dozens or more of additional BSDs (again, of various Ranks) and allies that will be on call for a place like this.<br /> <br /> And none of this is to say a level 5 Hive can't be taken down. That isn't an argument I'm making. But writing it off as a simple endeavor is doing a disservice to what level 5 Caerns/Hives actually are. They are places that godlike beings of the Umbra have personal stakes in.<br /> <br /> Caerns are not just &quot;a place of religious observance&quot;. They are also military training facilities, portals to other Realms and beings, social focal points (for both Garou and Spirits) and near-instant gateways to other Caerns across the world. A Level 5 Hive/Caern can call in defenders from literally almost anywhere in the world. I would expect to have to wade through hundreds of Spirals (without counting other defenders) to destroy one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T15:06:45-07:00","id":1134965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134953#post1134953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...) A Level 5 Hive/Caern can call in defenders from literally almost anywhere in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>How often does a Level 5 Caern or Hive fall to outside forces? A few every century? Or more like a few every half a millennium? Or something in between?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T16:19:53-07:00","id":1134988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134892#post1134892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't we, though? For what I take in this thread, that single Hive seems to be the neuralgic center of Wyrm operations in Earth, revered by all BSD. It probably can count with the Masters of Malfean Nephandi as &quot;minions&quot;, while counting with help of the entirety of Pentex.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's one way of looking at things, but it isn't how WtA presents things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134906#post1134906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a handful of level 5 Hives in the entire world (I wouldn't say more than 3).</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing really indicates them being that rare.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And this discussion would have me to believe that they exist purely because the Technocracy doesn't see them as worth their time. But if for some reason they did, that these places would (relatively) easily be cleansed. </div> </div> </div>Actually, as I've tried to reiterate, is that the Technocracy doesn't actually understand the threat they pose. Not that they think it's beneath them, but that werewolves huddling around their nodes is usually not a threat to the Union's goals, and that gives Garou (of any affiliation) space to not have to worry about Union attacks. If the Union realized what a level 5 Hive represents, they'd be very likely to try to take it out, and they'd be very likely to win because once they decided to move, they move with overwhelming force and tools the BSDs just aren't equipped to deal with in time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And saying that the cost is high, but that it comes out of stockpiles that can be refilled at some later date. And that said resources have no definite amount. This to me makes the &quot;high&quot; cost meaningless. </div> </div> </div>Eh? I don't think this is either fair, or has much of a point. These are games. We're not going to get a 1K page technical text detailing the complex inner workings of the Technocratic bureaucracy. The books provide the details we need, just like we're not getting stats for higher level spirits. We're just given an idea of their power and their limitations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is no reason the Technocracy shouldn't have eradicated (or claimed and cleansed) all non-Mage strongholds if this we're the case. </div> </div> </div>Sure there are:<br /> <br /> 1) The Technocracy can be stopped by the cosmic powers of the setting. If Luna steps in to protect the Fera, she's going to win a magic-off with the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> 2) The Technocracy also has other mages to worry about. If they expend all their forces trying to wipe out all non-mage RDs, they're giving the Traditions the chance of centuries to counter attack and change the course of the Ascension War/related conflicts. Plus the Nephandi aren't going to sit back while that's happening and do nothing, including getting some of their dark masters into this world without the VEs running around putting stops to such incursions.<br /> <br /> 3) The Technocracy's rise to this level of power is relatively recent. They haven't had the level of power they've had in during the &quot;now&quot; of the books for more than a hundred years or so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are other superpowers that have a vested interest in NK that are comparable to the US. This isn't the case with this comparison. You don't have the Council of 9 aligned with the Garou or Vampires to protect them from the Technocracy. </div> </div> </div>See above. The Technocracy isn't actually a match for beings like the Incarnae and Celestines in their full power, and many supernaturals do have connections to such beings. And even if the Traditions aren't actively alligned with the Garou, they're not going to pass up chances to attack the Union if the Union commits too much to other enemies.<br /> <br /> Yes, the US vs. NK example isn't perfect, but no analogy is perfect. It's close enough to actually explain the setting as is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eh. Just how I see this. And the thread so far has mostly supported this view imo. And that sort of logic, in my mind, goes against the Setting as written. Specifically when you take into account the other game line's and not just looking at it from an exclusively Mage pov. </div> </div> </div>And it strongly feels like you're cherry picking to reach this conclusion rather than really engaging with what's being said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Other Supernaturals having extremely valuable resources the Technocracy would want (Caerns/Hives) does not. Not if they have the power to take said resources with little trouble or fear of effective retribution. </div> </div> </div>The Technocracy isn't in particular need of more Nodes, even level 5 Hive ones; especially since it's a huge investment to deal with the military operation to take it, and the clean up effort to make it viable for Technocratic use. Keep in mind, that Prime mages can make Nodes themselves. Unlike the Garou, they're not bound by existing potential Caern sites for new Nodes. Making Nodes has it's own issues but it's generally easier than taking them. So taking a Hive just for the Node is a bit pointless unless there's a bigger agenda at hand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can see the point you are making here, but I don't agree with the comparison. </div> </div> </div>And I continue to feel like this is a cop out. &quot;I don't like your analogy&quot; doesn't really do anything for the conversation. Neither does nitpicking where the analogy isn't perfect. If you can see the point I'm making, the comparison did the only job it was intended to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So their greatest strength is the ability to win any conflict that can be solved by killing your opponent? </div> </div> </div>Is that what I posted? Because you quoted my words, and these aren't what I said.<br /> <br /> Their greatest strength is their organizational power. They're more organized than any other faction out there. Which means they have the best logistics, and best ability to apply their maximum amount of force to a situation. That is not &quot;any conflict that can be solved by killing.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would argue that we're talking about one of the most powerful of the Wyrm's strongholds (if we are still using the level 5 Hive as the focal point of this discussion) outside of the Realm of Malfeas. </div> </div> </div>But it's still one stronghold against a military force that's designed to work on both sides of the Gauntlet and hit hard and fast with the power to blow up strongholds. The Technocracy had the power to take out Doisstep, and that's closer to Malfeas (being a mage built Umbral Realm with it's own Reality Zone they had to fight against, with an Archmage living there) than a level 5 Hive (esp. since it had multiple powerful Nodes supporting it).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134918#post1134918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hive/Caern Spirit alone, minus the army of defenders is going to be a being of immense power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing supports the Caern Totems as being this powerful for fighting for the Caern's protection. It takes considerable effort for Garou to get one to bless a single pack for a month. They're not anything to scoff at, but their power is mostly bound up in the Caern itself, and isn't free to unleash on things attacking like other potential defenders.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134953#post1134953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is in addition to whatever other defenses it's going to have from various Wyrm Fera, probably a Nephandi or 2 and other weirdness (Thunderwyrms, visiting Incarna, portals to other Realms, etc). And this is also in addition to the possible dozens or more of additional BSDs (again, of various Ranks) and allies that will be on call for a place like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other tainted Fera don't really change the equation.<br /> <br /> Nephandi aren't going to stick around to fight the Technocracy (even if they care about helping the BSDs, they know tipping off the Union to that means the Union and the Traditions might team up again which is worse for the Wyrm's forces in the long run; better to lose one Hive than lots of them).<br /> <br /> Incarnae don't just &quot;visit&quot; Caerns.<br /> <br /> Caerns generally do not have portals to other Realms laying around, even level 5 ones.<br /> <br /> Moon Bridges to other Hives take time to open, take time to use and you need to rely the call for help on top of transit times (that whole &quot;near instant&quot; really isn't accurate even if it's fast), and the pathstones are subject to damage or interference. They are great if the Hive knows the kind of attack that's about to happen, but they're effectively pointless if the Union catches the BSDs unaware (and the BSDs aren't exactly in a great position to see it coming).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But writing it off as a simple endeavor is doing a disservice to what level 5 Caerns/Hives actually are. </div> </div> </div>And claiming this is what we're doing is a disservice to the actual discussion. We're talking about the Technocracy mobilizing a fleet of Voidships, dozens of fully Enlightened Operatives from multiple areas of expertise, hundreds of extraordinary citizens and similar assets, and even more unaware proles. We're talking about the Hive's defenders finding themselves carpet bombed out of the blue with hypertech ordinance designed specifically to interfere with their spirit based powers, while drones fire silver loaded cluster munitions as specific targets.<br /> <br /> This might be &quot;easy&quot; for the Union to accomplish, but it's not simple.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would expect to have to wade through hundreds of Spirals (without counting other defenders) to destroy one. </div> </div> </div>Probably because you're thinking about what it takes for something like the Garou Nation to take on a Hive, where they can't marshal the needed forces as quickly, as stealthily, or as certain to avoid weakening their own defenses, as the Union can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T17:11:14-07:00","id":1134996,"title":"","content":"I tend to view the Technocracy as built on bravado. They can't beat the Traditions. Why would they be able to beat anyone else?<br /> <br /> I do think they could destroy Pentex if they wanted to but it would require ALL of their resources and take years as well as make them vulnerable to the Traditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T18:52:45-07:00","id":1135016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134996#post1134996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to view the Technocracy as built on bravado. They can't beat the Traditions. Why would they be able to beat anyone else?<br /> <br /> I do think they could destroy Pentex if they wanted to but it would require ALL of their resources and take years as well as make them vulnerable to the Traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>They did beat the Traditions. Then the game changed. Now they have to take and hold territory. Winning the hearts and minds of the people rather than just smashing the oppressive structures of yore beneath Musketfire and Cannons.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the Traditions can hide in the shadows. Slipping things into the consensus here or there. Using the unions own methods of communication against them. Rather than having to BUILD anything of their own, the Traditions merely have to destroy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T19:12:28-07:00","id":1135022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1134627#post1134627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mind you, if the Technocracy could do that, they wouldn't need the Men in Black or HIT Marks.<br /> <br /> Remember, the Technocracy never can do Vulgar Magic.<br /> <br /> They always need foci and a Correspondence 2/Forces 2/Prime 2 rote is a Drone strike.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> The can use Vulgar magic as much as they want to. They can use it in front of Witnesses. They can use it on a train. They can use it in the rain. In a box. With a fox. <br /> <br /> Evidence.... Every HIT MARK or particle accelerator cannon. Every mutant monster or iterative clone bank for essential personel. The great Market Adjustment of 2008. Panopticon strike teams doing pretty much everything. Taking out an Antediluvian with orbital mirrors and and spirit-pumped nukes. And so on and so on and so on.<br /> <br /> They have the EDGE when doing Coincidental effects because they've convinced most everyone their way works. But that doesn't mean they CAN'T do Vulgar. It just means more paperwork explaining why it was necessary. <br /> <br /> A drone strike might make it easier, but it's not going to get the job done, at least not effectively, but defending the Consensus against this Hive/Pit/BSD nightmare carnival (with extra sandwyrm-y goodness!) is worth the red tape. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T19:40:52-07:00","id":1135030,"title":"","content":"Indeed, they can go Vulgar. They even have Procedures that are ALWAYS Vulgar<br /> <br /> They just shy from it's use, mostly because it's dangerous. You need to get autorization to use Vulgar stuff.<br /> <br /> But when the mother of the evil Nodes it's there to be sanitized, I think you can get autorization to do pretty much whatever you think it's necessary, just don't ruin the Masquerade too much<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to view the Technocracy as built on bravado. They can't beat the Traditions. Why would they be able to beat anyone else?</div> </div> </div> </div>XDXDXDXD..<br /> <br /> Although Enginseer it's right, they kinda beat the Traditions at the beginning of Revised (the Fall of Horizon marks their victory, but the Traditions had been in a LONG losing streak before that). They just weren't able to eradicate them. Now they're too disorganized to do that thanks to the Anomaly, Threat Null, and the Civil War. And they're kinda infiltrated by Nephandi, but who isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T19:41:56-07:00","id":1135031,"title":"","content":"Eh, they went back and forth between &quot;The Technocracy won the war&quot; and &quot;Both sides lost.&quot;<br /> <br /> So I split the difference with a Pyrrhic victory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T22:36:46-07:00","id":1135074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1135030#post1135030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Indeed, they can go Vulgar. They even have Procedures that are ALWAYS Vulgar</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not something special in itself. There are Mystic Rotes which are always Vulgar. Mystics can go Vulgar, as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1135030#post1135030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They just shy from it's use, mostly because it's dangerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>And because of all the other reasons True Mages might avoid casting Vulgar Effects. It's harder, for example. Another reason is that it is bad for maintaining subtlety and secrecy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 08-29-2017, 01:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T04:06:45-07:00","id":1135119,"title":"","content":"I find it interesting that this thread seems to treat this all as a very strategic 'Technocracy sends in as much as is necessary' situation. In any game I ran, the Technocracy moving against a Hive would be a local Construct trying to work out if they had the resources necessary for this. 4-8 Enlightened Scientists &amp; 20-40 lightly enhanced Citizens (Extraordinary or otherwise), perhaps? Up against 2-4 packs (6-20 BSDs) in the sept &amp; perhaps a dozen spirits bargained with for the protection of the Hive; maybe even some support from Pentex, depending on the circumstances.<br /> <br /> That to me sounds like the Union might be able to win, but at a lot of risk and <i>certainly</i> not without putting everything else they were working on at risk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T06:03:44-07:00","id":1135137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yue Ryong</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1135119#post1135119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it interesting that this thread seems to treat this all as a very strategic 'Technocracy sends in as much as is necessary' situation. In any game I ran, the Technocracy moving against a Hive would be a local Construct trying to work out if they had the resources necessary for this. 4-8 Enlightened Scientists &amp; 20-40 lightly enhanced Citizens (Extraordinary or otherwise), perhaps? Up against 2-4 packs (6-20 BSDs) in the sept &amp; perhaps a dozen spirits bargained with for the protection of the Hive; maybe even some support from Pentex, depending on the circumstances.<br /> <br /> That to me sounds like the Union might be able to win, but at a lot of risk and <i>certainly</i> not without putting everything else they were working on at risk.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the way the Technocracy works unless a time crunch means waiting for reinforcements is detrimental.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T08:01:46-07:00","id":1135154,"title":"","content":"Or unless they think that they can neutralize the Hive without calling for help. Technocracy does expect an Amalgam to take initiative if they can solve the problem without much risk. You shouldn't take unnecessary risks, but you can't call the local Symposium each time you discover a vampire, otherwise your superiors will think you're not up to the task of elevating and protecting mankind.<br /> <br /> Asses the danger of the Pit could be a mission issued to an Amalgam of the local Construct. After that you need to think about how to eliminate the threat expending the minimum amount of resources possible because otherwise the other Technocrats start complaining...Sure it would be nice to have a lot of Voidships firing photon torpedoes to the Hive, but VE would much rather have those fighting against that Treath they refuse to mention, Sure, the Syndicate have resources, but those would be much better spent elsewhere to increase proffit. Technocracy sending reinforcements shouldn't be taken for granted, the fact that you can ask for this kind of reinforcement and that you WILL get them if you can make your case already sets them appart from any other supernatural group.<br /> <br /> If you cannot convince your superiors that the Hive it's a serious enough a threath, they won't send the reinforcements. This is where Technocracy general blindness to the Midde Umbra and BSD trully enters in play. Even if you discover the Hive, your superiors would be like: Werewolves, our projections show that they will be extint in the next decade or so...do not waste resources unless they really start screwing things up. You would need to be very convincing about the danger such a Hive represents if you want them to send the necessary force. That, in itself, could be a Technocratic adventure, where the peril would be to underestimate the Hive and/or fail to produce good enough evidence (or if a Technepandi intercepts it, and arranges your death).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-29-2017, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T07:44:51-07:00","id":1135442,"title":"","content":"Also, depending on the sort of guy or girl leading the local Amalgams, it could be an opportunity to demonstrate one's skills and Enlightenment (or, in Etherite parlance: &quot;to make all those fools at the university regret my expulsion!&quot;).<br /> <br /> For example - I could imagine a VE leading the local Technocrats testing out his new Local Reality Anchor devices on the Hive. At several precisely calculated &quot;Lagrange points&quot; surrounding the Hive, Anchors are installed within a reinforced building and fed from onsite Matrices. They progressively raise the Gauntlet in an expanding area, eventually asserting material reality at the aberration within the tunnels. Now, if he comes back to the Symposium, not only has he removed a number of dangerous shapeshifting Reality Deviants and repaired a breach in the all-important Gauntlet, he also designed the hypertech, the efficacy of which was just demonstrated! Cue the funding.<br /> <br /> (That's not to say this particular idea is awesome on its own - BSDs would have no problem breaking into a random Technocratic outpost and shredding the inhabitants. This guy would also need some powerful Mind fields preventing them from acknowledging its existence, or Correspondence-enhanced doors that only lead to the actual interior of the building when the correct Procedures are engaged.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T17:04:57-07:00","id":1135638,"title":"","content":"As far as the Technocracy and Pentex are concerned, I always thought in white room combat, the Pentex would win pretty convincingly. If this were more of a strategic battle, the Technocrats would win easily. <br /> <br /> But my knowledge from this comes from educated(and uneducated guesswork) and other rpg forums who've wondered the same thing as me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T19:29:10-07:00","id":1135660,"title":"","content":"Forgive the roundbout answer, I think it's worth reading in answer to the question.<br /> <br /> If you want to go with a full crossover, then the setting you create is what counts.<br /> <br /> When allowing werewolf elements into my mage game, I make the worm a known threat to the Void Engineers, they treat it very seriously, as do many of the Progenitors, and even some members of the other conventions.<br /> <br /> The Garou are thought of as a unique and highly resilient breed of Reality Deviants who are deeply entrenched in a culture of cognitive dissonance and religious fanaticism which may or may not be the result of genetic or innate qualities. <br /> <br /> The Techoncracy WOULD see the Garou as worthy of extermination, particularly because the Garou value nodes in the extreme and have a strongly possessive belief regarding them, to the point where they will sometimes become maliciously violent towards constructs and personnel attached to said nodes.<br /> <br /> However, the Garou are also deeply dedicated to the destruction of the worm (also known as Extra-Dimension Entity insert code-name here), as such, there are some theories among fringe technocrats that the 'Garou' are possibly a natural immune system within reality and that they exist to destroy the worm. More common is simply the belief that they should simply be allowed to continue to exist and used as a proxy against the worm, an entity which the Garou appear to be very well equipped to fight. Even if they contaminate the gene pool and practice a religious crusade of irrationally radical environmentalism.<br /> <br /> This brings me to my answer to your question. The Garou nation is a reckless and dangerous cult of fanatics, they do however obey what they call &quot;the Veil,&quot; a self policing mechanism that prevents them from violating the consensus in many cases. Should elements of the Garou nation come to violate the veil too frequently, they simply require an 'adjustment' to steer them back to their standard operating procedures. Provided they don't become too much of a liability (and if weren't for the work they do in keeping the worm in check, they would be WAY too much of a liability), they can be allowed to continue their religious crusade on their own terms... mostly.<br /> <br /> And when the Tehcnocracy finds out about a Worm Pit, well, it just forwards that information on to... certain relevant parties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T19:51:33-07:00","id":1135662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1135660#post1135660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive the roundbout answer, I think it's worth reading in answer to the question.<br /> <br /> If you want to go with a full crossover, then the setting you create is what counts.<br /> <br /> When allowing werewolf elements into my mage game, I make the worm a known threat to the Void Engineers, they treat it very seriously, as do many of the Progenitors, and even some members of the other conventions.<br /> <br /> The Garou are thought of as a unique and highly resilient breed of Reality Deviants who are deeply entrenched in a culture of cognitive dissonance and religious fanaticism which may or may not be the result of genetic or innate qualities.<br /> <br /> The Techoncracy WOULD see the Garou as worthy of extermination, particularly because the Garou value nodes in the extreme and have a strongly possessive belief regarding them, to the point where they will sometimes become maliciously violent towards constructs and personnel attached to said nodes.<br /> <br /> However, the Garou are also deeply dedicated to the destruction of the worm (also known as Extra-Dimension Entity insert code-name here), as such, there are some theories among fringe technocrats that the 'Garou' are possibly a natural immune system within reality and that they exist to destroy the worm. More common is simply the belief that they should simply be allowed to continue to exist and used as a proxy against the worm, an entity which the Garou appear to be very well equipped to fight. Even if they contaminate the gene pool and practice a religious crusade of irrationally radical environmentalism.<br /> <br /> This brings me to my answer to your question. The Garou nation is a reckless and dangerous cult of fanatics, they do however obey what they call &quot;the Veil,&quot; a self policing mechanism that prevents them from violating the consensus in many cases. Should elements of the Garou nation come to violate the veil too frequently, they simply require an 'adjustment' to steer them back to their standard operating procedures. Provided they don't become too much of a liability (and if weren't for the work they do in keeping the worm in check, they would be WAY too much of a liability), they can be allowed to continue their religious crusade on their own terms... mostly.<br /> <br /> And when the Tehcnocracy finds out about a Worm Pit, well, it just forwards that information on to... certain relevant parties.</div> </div> </div> </div>One wonders just how much the Union would freak out if they found out they were living in a Prince of Darkness-esque existence and one or two members of every Amalgalm showed up like in <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iY-QBvy3lR8\" target=\"_blank\">this scene</a> to deliver ominous warnings to their former colleagues every so often.<br /> <br /> (I'm not really stretching things for the established lore of various WoD sources, either. Check the end of the Book of the Weaver's second chapter. And it's suggested that the capacities for control and destruction that you see in the movie could be matched by a tiny piece of the Wyrm, the Talon Thrassus Thrice-Damned)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T14:36:11-07:00","id":1135932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1133838#post1133838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most perceived problems of crossover come because one assumes that *my* magical thing it's going to be super effective just because nothing says it won't. Ignoring that the material most likely wasn't written with every game-line and every situation in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this. The cWoD was explicitly not constructed to operate as a unified narrative. Even within the same game line the books contradict each other, and there are loads of sidebars encouraging players to disregard the metaplot and anything else that doesn't work for their game. At no point did someone review the mechanical underpinnings of all WoD material with an eye to them working together out of the box (and WW isn't well-known for mechanical rigor in any case). Every piece of fiction in which X supernatural wrecks Y number of Z supernatural was written because it seemed cool to the writers at the time. Even when WW literally ended the world they didn't provide a unified narrative. Werewolves got their Apocalypse. Mages got Ascension. Vampires had Gehenna. Most everyone else got Time of Judgment.<br /> <br /> Q: Who wins in an all-out fight between tons of Wyrm-slaves and tons of Technocrats?<br /> A: Whatever advances the narrative and is fun for my current group of players. Most likely answer is &quot;everyone loses, particularly the world at large.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T15:02:07-07:00","id":1135946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1135932#post1135932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At no point did someone review the mechanical underpinnings of all WoD material with an eye to them working together out of the box (and WW isn't well-known for mechanical rigor in any case).</div> </div> </div> </div>Quoted for Truth.<br /> <br /> It took me a bit just to get past the fluff exposition and actually start reading the rules... but then I was rather struck by the writers rather.... dickish and nonsensical ideas of the way certain things should work.<br /> <br /> Like.... &quot;Let's make Wonders of all stripes stupidly powerful in forged by dragons fire. How are we going to balance this? Force people to waste game night time sitting out of the game while everyone stares at their cheating powergaming self. Crafting magical items. HMMF.&quot;<br /> <br /> Each of the books seems more or less to be written on train of thought mind to page info vomit with little to no refining.<br /> <br /> Which, is great for the fluff. But the crunch suffers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T09:54:02-07:00","id":1137726,"title":"","content":"It helps if you toss the Union information on Wyrm-tainted corporations and couch it in terms of Nephandic influence. Then again, our group has the advantage of serious amounts of Occult Lore. We told them about Special Projects Division.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T08:18:58-07:00","id":1146341,"title":"","content":"But really, why the Iteration X and the Void Engineers do not nuke every Caern, Pit, Hive and Labyrinth from Orbit? It is the simplest and most effective and inexpensive method to dispatch Nephandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T08:27:53-07:00","id":1146348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1146341#post1146341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But really, why the Iteration X and the Void Engineers do not nuke every Caern, Pit, Hive and Labyrinth from Orbit? It is the simplest and most effective and inexpensive method to dispatch Nephandi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Waste of time and resources.<br /> <br /> Picture the war between the Technocracy and deviant like it's taking place on an old crumbling wooden platform out in the ocean.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy is at present holding the ground it has while it builds new steel platforms beneath the wood. On the surface it looks like they're doing nothing, but one day the work will be completed and they can tip the rest of the wooden platform, and all the superstionists who cling to it, into the sea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11744,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","user":"Enginseer-42","date":". 10-03-2017, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T20:45:55-07:00","id":1146553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1146348#post1146348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Waste of time and resources.<br /> <br /> Picture the war between the Technocracy and deviant like it's taking place on an old crumbling wooden platform out in the ocean.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy is at present holding the ground it has while it builds new steel platforms beneath the wood. On the surface it looks like they're doing nothing, but one day the work will be completed and they can tip the rest of the wooden platform, and all the superstionists who cling to it, into the sea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny that you mention the ocean, because Chulorviah, alone, present a substantially greater threat to mages than, say, changers. Changers can keep the infection at bay and purge it with a level one rite (Rokea are completely immune); mages, on the other hand. require high levels of both Spirit and Life to make an attempt at treating it. The Technocracy also has business in the undersea with the EFD and the Deepwater platform, explicitly a Chulorvian breeding ground and recruitment center per Blood-Dimmed Tides. Even an innocuous tropical vacation or meeting can provide an avenue of infection and organizational subversion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T03:37:01-07:00","id":1146599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1146553#post1146553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Funny that you mention the ocean, because Chulorviah, alone, present a substantially greater threat to mages than, say, changers. Changers can keep the infection at bay and purge it with a level one rite (Rokea are completely immune); mages, on the other hand. require high levels of both Spirit and Life to make an attempt at treating it. The Technocracy also has business in the undersea with the EFD and the Deepwater platform, explicitly a Chulorvian breeding ground and recruitment center per Blood-Dimmed Tides. Even an innocuous tropical vacation or meeting can provide an avenue of infection and organizational subversion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is Blood-Dimmed Tides Canon? Since 1) it is a crossover book and 2) Its contents pretty much contradicts with every other supplement of respective game, though admittedly The Infinite Tapestry(oh, that <i>gross </i>book...) cross-confirms Chulorviah's existence in Mage setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T08:42:53-07:00","id":1146691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133232-technocracy-vs-black-spiral-dancers?p=1146599#post1146599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Blood-Dimmed Tides Canon? Since 1) it is a crossover book and 2) Its contents pretty much contradicts with every other supplement of respective game, though admittedly The Infinite Tapestry(oh, that <i>gross </i>book...) cross-confirms Chulorviah's existence in Mage setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chulorviah were also added to W20 Book of the Wyrm, and the mer are fully integrated with C20 along with reworked versions of various Arts that first showed up there, so I'd say that most parts of BDT are probably canonical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":